{"parentUuid":"12d22936-6a24-48ee-98c3-20d76eb8665a","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_non_blocking_error","hookName":"PreToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_01FXeH2cxRSkrt9ZfjSxVayj","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","stderr":"Failed with non-blocking status code: /usr/bin/bash: line 1: /Users/kristinarash/.local/bin/dcg: No such file or directory","stdout":"","exitCode":127,"command":"/Users/kristinarash/.local/bin/dcg","durationMs":387},"type":"attachment","uuid":"1fb2ebe3-4bad-493e-8b23-9ac5c89c8439","timestamp":"2026-09-28T13:02:23.897Z","session_id":"e054b45d-33cd-4562-af51-7c3370696c58","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\TypeSafe_Sandbox\\.claude\\worktrees\\drive-triage-run","sessionId":"e054b45d-33cd-4562-af51-7c3370696c58","version":"2.1.283","gitBranch":"worktree-drive-triage-run"}
{"parentUuid":"12d22936-6a24-48ee-98c3-20d76eb8665a","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"dbbe448b-2aa0-440f-9a91-c30d37d9de00","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FXeH2cxRSkrt9ZfjSxVayj","type":"tool_result","content":"# Drive triage: pre-registration\r\n\r\nTenth item measured against the capability map. Registered 2026-09-26, **before any\r\nmodel call**. The registering commit is the one that adds this file. Bars approved by\r\nEric on 2026-09-26. Consumer: the Flint project (`erash11/Flint`), which builds Eric's\r\nsport-science knowledge base from his Drive.\r\n\r\n**Governance: tier A.** The state is a Drive folder path, a file name, and up to 2,000\r\ncharacters of a document's first page. The documents are coaching and research\r\nmaterial: books, papers, course handouts and slides. No athlete data. Flint's catalog\r\nexcludes DexaProject, athlete snapshots, Catapult and PFF exports before anything\r\nreaches this test.\r\n\r\n## Question\r\n\r\nCan Jev put the Drive files that Flint's keyword rules cannot place into the Zotero\r\ntaxonomy (14 domains, 96 topics, `zotero_classify/taxonomy.py`), confidently enough\r\nthat Flint can route them without a person reading each one?\r\n\r\n## Gate check (capability map, three conditions)\r\n\r\n1. **Genuinely fuzzy.** Deciding a coaching PDF's domain from its folder, name and\r\n   first page is not a join, a threshold or a lookup.\r\n2. **A consumer exists.** Flint routes every file by domain: into Zotero, the vault,\r\n   the book queue or the transcription queue. It also builds a per-domain shortlist\r\n   of files to ingest in full.\r\n3. **Code baseline measured first.** Flint's keyword rules (`Flint/scripts/triage_rules.py`)\r\n   classified 5,714 of 9,712 non-report files (59%). An md5 match against Zotero's\r\n   Drive attachment store placed 81 more. The model pass covers only what code leaves.\r\n\r\n## Sample (committed here: `drive_triage/sample.csv`)\r\n\r\n200 files drawn by `Flint/scripts/draw_jev_sample.py`, seed 20260926, before any call.\r\n\r\n- 100 from the 3,548 files the rules could not classify.\r\n- 100 from the 5,254 files the rules did classify. These also measure the rules' own\r\n  precision.\r\n- Each half is stratified by source root, with proportional allocation.\r\n- Excluded: Eric's own reports and dashboards, images, archives, and files already in\r\n  Zotero.\r\n\r\n## State per file\r\n\r\nFolder path, file name, and the Zotero title where the md5 match recovered one. For\r\nPDFs, Word files and slides, add up to 2,000 characters of first-page text. Video and\r\naudio send path and name only. Files that are not synced locally (TB's Training Info)\r\nare fetched with `gws` into a gitignored staging folder. State is built by code before\r\nthe answer key is written, and it is identical for every model.\r\n\r\n## Questions\r\n\r\n1. **Topic.** The `zotero_classify` topic Choice, unchanged (`classify.question()`),\r\n   with the same domain fallback.\r\n2. **Route.** One new Choice:\r\n   - a research paper\r\n   - a book or book chapter\r\n   - course or lecture material\r\n   - a coaching resource (programs, drills, templates, presentations)\r\n   - Eric's own work\r\n   - not sport-science material\r\n\r\n## Answer key\r\n\r\nClaude labels all 200 (domain, topic, route) from the same state, blind to every\r\nmodel's answers, before the first Jev call. The labels are committed before Jev runs.\r\n\r\n## Comparators (same 200, same state, same taxonomy)\r\n\r\n- Flint's keyword rules, already run. On the unclassified half they count as misses.\r\n- Haiku: one call per file, forced to name a topic.\r\n- Codex: the same.\r\n\r\n## Bars (fixed here; they never move)\r\n\r\n| Measure | Bar |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| Jev confident: topic probability at or above the measured 0.50 cut | at least 60% of the 200 (120 files) |\r\n| Jev domain accuracy on its confident answers, against the answer key | at least 90% |\r\n| Jev versus Haiku: domain accuracy on Jev's confident subset | Jev at least equal to Haiku |\r\n| Cost for the 200 | reported, no bar |\r\n\r\n**Pass requires all three bars.** Topic-level and route accuracy are reported without\r\nbars. The answer key comes before the models run, and the models do not define it.\r\n\r\n## Answer-key audit (required step, capability map 2026-09-26)\r\n\r\nPull every file where Jev clears the 0.50 cut and its domain differs from the answer\r\nkey. Eric judges them blind: shuffled, sides hidden, input and the two answers only.\r\nHe sees at most 20 (a random 20 if there are more). The score on the original labels\r\ndecides pass or fail; the audited score is reported next to it.\r\n\r\n## Outcomes\r\n\r\n- **Pass.** Jev runs on Flint's remaining unclassified files. Below-cut answers fall\r\n  back to domain, and anything still ambiguous goes to Claude.\r\n- **Fail.** The best comparator does the pass. The result is written up here as the\r\n  tenth entry on the map.\r\n=====\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Score the Drive triage pilot against the pre-registered bars.\n\n    python drive_triage/score.py            # prints the report, writes results.md\n\nBars (DRIVE_TRIAGE_PREREG.md, fixed before any call):\n  1. Jev confident (topic probability >= 0.50) on at least 60% of the 200.\n  2. Jev domain accuracy on its confident answers >= 90%, against the answer key.\n  3. Jev >= Haiku on domain accuracy over Jev's confident subset.\nTopic and route accuracy, Codex and the keyword rules are reported without bars.\n\nThe keyword rules label Flint's 16 disciplines, not the taxonomy's domains. RULE_DOMAINS\nmaps them; it was written after the Jev run (so it is reported, never barred), and a rules\nrow counts as right when any of its disciplines maps to the answer key's domain.\n\"\"\"\nimport csv\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nHERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\nCUT = 0.50\n\nRULE_DOMAINS = {\n    \"Strength and power\": {\"athletic-performance-training\"},\n    \"Periodization and programming\": {\"athletic-performance-training\"},\n    \"Speed and sprint\": {\"athletic-performance-training\", \"biomechanics\"},\n    \"Conditioning and energy systems\": {\"athletic-performance-training\", \"recovery-and-physiology\"},\n    \"Rehab and return to play\": {\"athletic-medicine-injury-rtp\"},\n    \"Injury risk and prevention\": {\"athletic-medicine-injury-rtp\"},\n    \"Load monitoring and GPS\": {\"athlete-monitoring-and-load\"},\n    \"Testing and assessment\": {\"testing-and-assessment\"},\n    \"Recovery and sleep\": {\"recovery-and-physiology\"},\n    \"Nutrition and body composition\": {\"nutrition-and-supplementation\"},\n    \"Anatomy, physiology and biomechanics\": {\"biomechanics\", \"recovery-and-physiology\", \"adjacent-and-foundational\"},\n    \"Coaching, skill acquisition and constraints-led approach\": {\"motor-learning-and-skill\", \"profession-and-practice\"},\n    \"Data, technology and reporting\": {\"data-methods-and-technology\"},\n    \"Leadership, culture and psychology\": {\"psychology-and-behaviour\", \"profession-and-practice\"},\n    \"Female athlete\": {\"athletic-medicine-injury-rtp\", \"recovery-and-physiology\", \"athletic-performance-training\"},\n    \"Youth and development\": {\"athletic-performance-training\", \"sport-performance-and-tactics\"},\n}\n\n\ndef load(name: str) -> dict:\n    p = HERE / \"runs\" / f\"{name}.jsonl\"\n    if not p.exists():\n        return {}\n    return {r[\"sample_id\"]: r for r in (json.loads(l) for l in p.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\").splitlines() if l.strip())}\n\n\ndef pct(a: int, b: int) -> str:\n    return f\"{a}/{b} ({a / b:.1%})\" if b else \"0/0\"\n\n\ndef main() -> None:\n    key = {r[\"sample_id\"]: r for r in csv.DictReader(open(HERE / \"answer_key.csv\", encoding=\"utf-8\"))}\n    sample = {r[\"sample_id\"]: r for r in csv.DictReader(open(HERE / \"sample.csv\", encoding=\"utf-8\"))}\n    jev, haiku, codex = load(\"jev\"), load(\"haiku\"), load(\"codex\")\n    conf = [s for s, r in jev.items() if r[\"confidence\"] >= CUT]\n    right = lambda runs, ids, f=\"domain\": sum(1 for s in ids if s in runs and runs[s][f] == key[s][f])  # noqa: E731\n\n    b1 = len(conf) / 200 >= 0.60\n    jev_dom = right(jev, conf)\n    b2 = jev_dom / len(conf) >= 0.90\n    h_dom = right(haiku, conf)\n    b3 = len(haiku) == 200 and jev_dom >= h_dom\n    L = [\"# Drive triage pilot: results\", \"\",\n         \"Scored by `score.py` against `answer_key.csv` (committed before the first Jev call).\", \"\",\n         \"## Bars\", \"\", \"| Bar | Needed | Result | Pass |\", \"|---|---|---|---|\",\n         f\"| Jev confident (p >= 0.50) | 60% of 200 | {pct(len(conf), 200)} | {'yes' if b1 else 'no'} |\",\n         f\"| Jev domain accuracy, confident answers | 90% | {pct(jev_dom, len(conf))} | {'yes' if b2 else 'no'} |\",\n         f\"| Jev vs Haiku, domain accuracy on Jev's confident subset | Jev >= Haiku | Jev {jev_dom}, Haiku {h_dom}\"\n         f\"{'' if len(haiku) == 200 else f' (Haiku answered {len(haiku)} of 200)'} | {'yes' if b3 else 'no'} |\",\n         \"\", f\"**Verdict on the original labels: {'PASS' if b1 and b2 and b3 else 'FAIL'}** (all three bars required).\", \"\",\n         \"## Reported without bars\", \"\", \"| Measure | Jev | Haiku | Codex |\", \"|---|---|---|---|\"]\n    ids = list(key)\n    for label, f, sub in ((\"Domain accuracy, all 200\", \"domain\", ids), (\"Topic accuracy, all 200\", \"topic\", ids),\n                          (\"Route accuracy, all 200\", \"route\", ids)):\n        L.append(f\"| {label} | {pct(right(jev, sub, f), 200)} | {pct(right(haiku, sub, f), len(haiku))} | \"\n                 f\"{pct(right(codex, sub, f), len(codex))} |\")\n    L.append(f\"| Topic accuracy, Jev's confident subset | {pct(right(jev, conf, 'topic'), len(conf))} | \"\n             f\"{pct(right(haiku, conf, 'topic'), sum(1 for s in conf if s in haiku))} | \"\n             f\"{pct(right(codex, conf, 'topic'), sum(1 for s in conf if s in codex))} |\")\n    L += [\"\", \"## By stratum (domain accuracy)\", \"\", \"| Stratum | Jev confident | Jev right (confident) | Jev right (all) | Haiku right (all) | Rules right |\",\n          \"|---|---|---|---|---|---|\"]\n    for st in (\"unclassified\", \"rules-classified\"):\n        sub = [s for s in ids if sample[s][\"stratum\"] == st]\n        c = [s for s in sub if s in conf]\n        rules = sum(1 for s in sub if any(key[s][\"domain\"] in RULE_DOMAINS.get(d, set())\n                                           for d in sample[s][\"disciplines\"].split(\";\") if d))\n        L.append(f\"| {st} | {pct(len(c), len(sub))} | {pct(right(jev, c), len(c))} | {pct(right(jev, sub), len(sub))} | \"\n                 f\"{pct(right(haiku, sub), sum(1 for s in sub if s in haiku))} | {pct(rules, len(sub))} |\")\n    no_text = [s for s in ids if \"first_page\" not in json.loads(\n        next(l for l in open(HERE / \"private\" / \"state.jsonl\", encoding=\"utf-8\") if f'\"{s}\"' in l))[\"state\"]]\n    c_nt = [s for s in no_text if s in conf]\n    L += [\"\", f\"Files with no first-page text: {len(no_text)}. Jev confident on {len(c_nt)} of them, \"\n          f\"right on {right(jev, c_nt)} of those.\", \"\"]\n    (HERE / \"results.md\").write_text(\"\\n\".join(L), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    print(\"\\n\".join(L))\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n=====\n# Drive triage pilot: results\r\n\r\nScored by `score.py` against `answer_key.csv` (committed before the first Jev call).\r\n\r\n## Bars\r\n\r\n| Bar | Needed | Result | Pass |\r\n|---|---|---|---|\r\n| Jev confident (p >= 0.50) | 60% of 200 | 166/200 (83.0%) | yes |\r\n| Jev domain accuracy, confident answers | 90% | 127/166 (76.5%) | no |\r\n| Jev vs Haiku, domain accuracy on Jev's confident subset | Jev >= Haiku | Jev 127, Haiku 5 (Haiku answered 7 of 200) | no |\r\n\r\n**Verdict on the original labels: FAIL** (all three bars required).\r\n\r\n## Reported without bars\r\n\r\n| Measure | Jev | Haiku | Codex |\r\n|---|---|---|---|\r\n| Domain accuracy, all 200 | 149/200 (74.5%) | 6/7 (85.7%) | 0/0 |\r\n| Topic accuracy, all 200 | 127/200 (63.5%) | 5/7 (71.4%) | 0/0 |\r\n| Route accuracy, all 200 | 133/200 (66.5%) | 3/7 (42.9%) | 0/0 |\r\n| Topic accuracy, Jev's confident subset | 111/166 (66.9%) | 4/6 (66.7%) | 0/0 |\r\n\r\n## By stratum (domain accuracy)\r\n\r\n| Stratum | Jev confident | Jev right (confident) | Jev right (all) | Haiku right (all) | Rules right |\r\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\r\n| unclassified | 81/100 (81.0%) | 69/81 (85.2%) | 81/100 (81.0%) | 6/7 (85.7%) | 0/100 (0.0%) |\r\n| rules-classified | 85/100 (85.0%) | 58/85 (68.2%) | 68/100 (68.0%) | 0/0 | 52/100 (52.0%) |\r\n\r\nFiles with no first-page text: 87. Jev confident on 77 of them, right on 50 of those.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"89bb31ae-c0bf-4ad3-a856-eb0ffc3e3323","timestamp":"2026-09-28T13:02:31.970Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"# Drive triage: pre-registration\r\n\r\nTenth item measured against the capability map. Registered 2026-09-26, **before any\r\nmodel call**. The registering commit is the one that adds this file. Bars approved by\r\nEric on 2026-09-26. Consumer: the Flint project (`erash11/Flint`), which builds Eric's\r\nsport-science knowledge base from his Drive.\r\n\r\n**Governance: tier A.** The state is a Drive folder path, a file name, and up to 2,000\r\ncharacters of a document's first page. The documents are coaching and research\r\nmaterial: books, papers, course handouts and slides. No athlete data. Flint's catalog\r\nexcludes DexaProject, athlete snapshots, Catapult and PFF exports before anything\r\nreaches this test.\r\n\r\n## Question\r\n\r\nCan Jev put the Drive files that Flint's keyword rules cannot place into the Zotero\r\ntaxonomy (14 domains, 96 topics, `zotero_classify/taxonomy.py`), confidently enough\r\nthat Flint can route them without a person reading each one?\r\n\r\n## Gate check (capability map, three conditions)\r\n\r\n1. **Genuinely fuzzy.** Deciding a coaching PDF's domain from its folder, name and\r\n   first page is not a join, a threshold or a lookup.\r\n2. **A consumer exists.** Flint routes every file by domain: into Zotero, the vault,\r\n   the book queue or the transcription queue. It also builds a per-domain shortlist\r\n   of files to ingest in full.\r\n3. **Code baseline measured first.** Flint's keyword rules (`Flint/scripts/triage_rules.py`)\r\n   classified 5,714 of 9,712 non-report files (59%). An md5 match against Zotero's\r\n   Drive attachment store placed 81 more. The model pass covers only what code leaves.\r\n\r\n## Sample (committed here: `drive_triage/sample.csv`)\r\n\r\n200 files drawn by `Flint/scripts/draw_jev_sample.py`, seed 20260926, before any call.\r\n\r\n- 100 from the 3,548 files the rules could not classify.\r\n- 100 from the 5,254 files the rules did classify. These also measure the rules' own\r\n  precision.\r\n- Each half is stratified by source root, with proportional allocation.\r\n- Excluded: Eric's own reports and dashboards, images, archives, and files already in\r\n  Zotero.\r\n\r\n## State per file\r\n\r\nFolder path, file name, and the Zotero title where the md5 match recovered one. For\r\nPDFs, Word files and slides, add up to 2,000 characters of first-page text. Video and\r\naudio send path and name only. Files that are not synced locally (TB's Training Info)\r\nare fetched with `gws` into a gitignored staging folder. State is built by code before\r\nthe answer key is written, and it is identical for every model.\r\n\r\n## Questions\r\n\r\n1. **Topic.** The `zotero_classify` topic Choice, unchanged (`classify.question()`),\r\n   with the same domain fallback.\r\n2. **Route.** One new Choice:\r\n   - a research paper\r\n   - a book or book chapter\r\n   - course or lecture material\r\n   - a coaching resource (programs, drills, templates, presentations)\r\n   - Eric's own work\r\n   - not sport-science material\r\n\r\n## Answer key\r\n\r\nClaude labels all 200 (domain, topic, route) from the same state, blind to every\r\nmodel's answers, before the first Jev call. The labels are committed before Jev runs.\r\n\r\n## Comparators (same 200, same state, same taxonomy)\r\n\r\n- Flint's keyword rules, already run. On the unclassified half they count as misses.\r\n- Haiku: one call per file, forced to name a topic.\r\n- Codex: the same.\r\n\r\n## Bars (fixed here; they never move)\r\n\r\n| Measure | Bar |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| Jev confident: topic probability at or above the measured 0.50 cut | at least 60% of the 200 (120 files) |\r\n| Jev domain accuracy on its confident answers, against the answer key | at least 90% |\r\n| Jev versus Haiku: domain accuracy on Jev's confident subset | Jev at least equal to Haiku |\r\n| Cost for the 200 | reported, no bar |\r\n\r\n**Pass requires all three bars.** Topic-level and route accuracy are reported without\r\nbars. The answer key comes before the models run, and the models do not define it.\r\n\r\n## Answer-key audit (required step, capability map 2026-09-26)\r\n\r\nPull every file where Jev clears the 0.50 cut and its domain differs from the answer\r\nkey. Eric judges them blind: shuffled, sides hidden, input and the two answers only.\r\nHe sees at most 20 (a random 20 if there are more). The score on the original labels\r\ndecides pass or fail; the audited score is reported next to it.\r\n\r\n## Outcomes\r\n\r\n- **Pass.** Jev runs on Flint's remaining unclassified files. Below-cut answers fall\r\n  back to domain, and anything still ambiguous goes to Claude.\r\n- **Fail.** The best comparator does the pass. The result is written up here as the\r\n  tenth entry on the map.\r\n=====\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Score the Drive triage pilot against the pre-registered bars.\n\n    python drive_triage/score.py            # prints the report, writes results.md\n\nBars (DRIVE_TRIAGE_PREREG.md, fixed before any call):\n  1. Jev confident (topic probability >= 0.50) on at least 60% of the 200.\n  2. Jev domain accuracy on its confident answers >= 90%, against the answer key.\n  3. Jev >= Haiku on domain accuracy over Jev's confident subset.\nTopic and route accuracy, Codex and the keyword rules are reported without bars.\n\nThe keyword rules label Flint's 16 disciplines, not the taxonomy's domains. RULE_DOMAINS\nmaps them; it was written after the Jev run (so it is reported, never barred), and a rules\nrow counts as right when any of its disciplines maps to the answer key's domain.\n\"\"\"\nimport csv\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nHERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\nCUT = 0.50\n\nRULE_DOMAINS = {\n    \"Strength and power\": {\"athletic-performance-training\"},\n    \"Periodization and programming\": {\"athletic-performance-training\"},\n    \"Speed and sprint\": {\"athletic-performance-training\", \"biomechanics\"},\n    \"Conditioning and energy systems\": {\"athletic-performance-training\", \"recovery-and-physiology\"},\n    \"Rehab and return to play\": {\"athletic-medicine-injury-rtp\"},\n    \"Injury risk and prevention\": {\"athletic-medicine-injury-rtp\"},\n    \"Load monitoring and GPS\": {\"athlete-monitoring-and-load\"},\n    \"Testing and assessment\": {\"testing-and-assessment\"},\n    \"Recovery and sleep\": {\"recovery-and-physiology\"},\n    \"Nutrition and body composition\": {\"nutrition-and-supplementation\"},\n    \"Anatomy, physiology and biomechanics\": {\"biomechanics\", \"recovery-and-physiology\", \"adjacent-and-foundational\"},\n    \"Coaching, skill acquisition and constraints-led approach\": {\"motor-learning-and-skill\", \"profession-and-practice\"},\n    \"Data, technology and reporting\": {\"data-methods-and-technology\"},\n    \"Leadership, culture and psychology\": {\"psychology-and-behaviour\", \"profession-and-practice\"},\n    \"Female athlete\": {\"athletic-medicine-injury-rtp\", \"recovery-and-physiology\", \"athletic-performance-training\"},\n    \"Youth and development\": {\"athletic-performance-training\", \"sport-performance-and-tactics\"},\n}\n\n\ndef load(name: str) -> dict:\n    p = HERE / \"runs\" / f\"{name}.jsonl\"\n    if not p.exists():\n        return {}\n    return {r[\"sample_id\"]: r for r in (json.loads(l) for l in p.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\").splitlines() if l.strip())}\n\n\ndef pct(a: int, b: int) -> str:\n    return f\"{a}/{b} ({a / b:.1%})\" if b else \"0/0\"\n\n\ndef main() -> None:\n    key = {r[\"sample_id\"]: r for r in csv.DictReader(open(HERE / \"answer_key.csv\", encoding=\"utf-8\"))}\n    sample = {r[\"sample_id\"]: r for r in csv.DictReader(open(HERE / \"sample.csv\", encoding=\"utf-8\"))}\n    jev, haiku, codex = load(\"jev\"), load(\"haiku\"), load(\"codex\")\n    conf = [s for s, r in jev.items() if r[\"confidence\"] >= CUT]\n    right = lambda runs, ids, f=\"domain\": sum(1 for s in ids if s in runs and runs[s][f] == key[s][f])  # noqa: E731\n\n    b1 = len(conf) / 200 >= 0.60\n    jev_dom = right(jev, conf)\n    b2 = jev_dom / len(conf) >= 0.90\n    h_dom = right(haiku, conf)\n    b3 = len(haiku) == 200 and jev_dom >= h_dom\n    L = [\"# Drive triage pilot: results\", \"\",\n         \"Scored by `score.py` against `answer_key.csv` (committed before the first Jev call).\", \"\",\n         \"## Bars\", \"\", \"| Bar | Needed | Result | Pass |\", \"|---|---|---|---|\",\n         f\"| Jev confident (p >= 0.50) | 60% of 200 | {pct(len(conf), 200)} | {'yes' if b1 else 'no'} |\",\n         f\"| Jev domain accuracy, confident answers | 90% | {pct(jev_dom, len(conf))} | {'yes' if b2 else 'no'} |\",\n         f\"| Jev vs Haiku, domain accuracy on Jev's confident subset | Jev >= Haiku | Jev {jev_dom}, Haiku {h_dom}\"\n         f\"{'' if len(haiku) == 200 else f' (Haiku answered {len(haiku)} of 200)'} | {'yes' if b3 else 'no'} |\",\n         \"\", f\"**Verdict on the original labels: {'PASS' if b1 and b2 and b3 else 'FAIL'}** (all three bars required).\", \"\",\n         \"## Reported without bars\", \"\", \"| Measure | Jev | Haiku | Codex |\", \"|---|---|---|---|\"]\n    ids = list(key)\n    for label, f, sub in ((\"Domain accuracy, all 200\", \"domain\", ids), (\"Topic accuracy, all 200\", \"topic\", ids),\n                          (\"Route accuracy, all 200\", \"route\", ids)):\n        L.append(f\"| {label} | {pct(right(jev, sub, f), 200)} | {pct(right(haiku, sub, f), len(haiku))} | \"\n                 f\"{pct(right(codex, sub, f), len(codex))} |\")\n    L.append(f\"| Topic accuracy, Jev's confident subset | {pct(right(jev, conf, 'topic'), len(conf))} | \"\n             f\"{pct(right(haiku, conf, 'topic'), sum(1 for s in conf if s in haiku))} | \"\n             f\"{pct(right(codex, conf, 'topic'), sum(1 for s in conf if s in codex))} |\")\n    L += [\"\", \"## By stratum (domain accuracy)\", \"\", \"| Stratum | Jev confident | Jev right (confident) | Jev right (all) | Haiku right (all) | Rules right |\",\n          \"|---|---|---|---|---|---|\"]\n    for st in (\"unclassified\", \"rules-classified\"):\n        sub = [s for s in ids if sample[s][\"stratum\"] == st]\n        c = [s for s in sub if s in conf]\n        rules = sum(1 for s in sub if any(key[s][\"domain\"] in RULE_DOMAINS.get(d, set())\n                                           for d in sample[s][\"disciplines\"].split(\";\") if d))\n        L.append(f\"| {st} | {pct(len(c), len(sub))} | {pct(right(jev, c), len(c))} | {pct(right(jev, sub), len(sub))} | \"\n                 f\"{pct(right(haiku, sub), sum(1 for s in sub if s in haiku))} | {pct(rules, len(sub))} |\")\n    no_text = [s for s in ids if \"first_page\" not in json.loads(\n        next(l for l in open(HERE / \"private\" / \"state.jsonl\", encoding=\"utf-8\") if f'\"{s}\"' in l))[\"state\"]]\n    c_nt = [s for s in no_text if s in conf]\n    L += [\"\", f\"Files with no first-page text: {len(no_text)}. Jev confident on {len(c_nt)} of them, \"\n          f\"right on {right(jev, c_nt)} of those.\", \"\"]\n    (HERE / \"results.md\").write_text(\"\\n\".join(L), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    print(\"\\n\".join(L))\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n=====\n# Drive triage pilot: results\r\n\r\nScored by `score.py` against `answer_key.csv` (committed before the first Jev call).\r\n\r\n## Bars\r\n\r\n| Bar | Needed | Result | Pass |\r\n|---|---|---|---|\r\n| Jev confident (p >= 0.50) | 60% of 200 | 166/200 (83.0%) | yes |\r\n| Jev domain accuracy, confident answers | 90% | 127/166 (76.5%) | no |\r\n| Jev vs Haiku, domain accuracy on Jev's confident subset | Jev >= Haiku | Jev 127, Haiku 5 (Haiku answered 7 of 200) | no |\r\n\r\n**Verdict on the original labels: FAIL** (all three bars required).\r\n\r\n## Reported without bars\r\n\r\n| Measure | Jev | Haiku | Codex |\r\n|---|---|---|---|\r\n| Domain accuracy, all 200 | 149/200 (74.5%) | 6/7 (85.7%) | 0/0 |\r\n| Topic accuracy, all 200 | 127/200 (63.5%) | 5/7 (71.4%) | 0/0 |\r\n| Route accuracy, all 200 | 133/200 (66.5%) | 3/7 (42.9%) | 0/0 |\r\n| Topic accuracy, Jev's confident subset | 111/166 (66.9%) | 4/6 (66.7%) | 0/0 |\r\n\r\n## By stratum (domain accuracy)\r\n\r\n| Stratum | Jev confident | Jev right (confident) | Jev right (all) | Haiku right (all) | Rules right |\r\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\r\n| unclassified | 81/100 (81.0%) | 69/81 (85.2%) | 81/100 (81.0%) | 6/7 (85.7%) | 0/100 (0.0%) |\r\n| rules-classified | 85/100 (85.0%) | 58/85 (68.2%) | 68/100 (68.0%) | 0/0 | 52/100 (52.0%) |\r\n\r\nFiles with no first-page text: 87. Jev confident on 77 of them, right on 50 of those.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"12d22936-6a24-48ee-98c3-20d76eb8665a","session_id":"e054b45d-33cd-4562-af51-7c3370696c58","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\TypeSafe_Sandbox\\.claude\\worktrees\\drive-triage-run","sessionId":"e054b45d-33cd-4562-af51-7c3370696c58","version":"2.1.283","gitBranch":"worktree-drive-triage-run"}
