{"parentUuid":"5a16392e-89f7-40e8-94e3-8a2dcc7846dc","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"dbbe448b-2aa0-440f-9a91-c30d37d9de00","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JCPy6NNnLBteK3y6C4Rp5R","type":"tool_result","content":"1:# STATUS\n5:## Current state\n6:- **2026-09-26 (Drive triage, REGISTERED, not run)**: tenth measurement. Can Jev place the Drive files Flint's keyword rules miss (3,548 of 9,712) into the Zotero taxonomy? Pre-registered in `docs/DRIVE_TRIAGE_PREREG.md` with the 200-file sample (`drive_triage/sample.csv`, seed 20260926). Bars were approved by Eric before any call: confident on at least 60%, domain accuracy at least 90% on the confident answers, and at least equal to Haiku. Next: build the state, then Claude's blind answer key, committed before the first Jev call. Consumer: `erash11/Flint`.\n17:- **2026-09-22 (spring exit notes → trajectory, CLOSED)**: **FAILS by 0.002, the ninth\n365:## Next\n419:## Open questions\n474:## Gotchas\n====\n1:# Jev capability map\n7:## Jev in one screen\n39:## Limits and failure modes\n78:## Where it fits what we run\n101:### PP_Recruiting: not now, and what would change that\n149:## What this unlocks that we cannot do today\n204:## Where not to use it\n221:## Sequence\n245:## Re-ranked 2026-09-20, after five items were resolved\n252:### The rule this project earned, stated as a gate rather than a story\n273:### Answer-key audit: a required step in every pre-registered test (added 2026-09-26)\n298:### Next three\n368:### Blocked on access, not on effort — and both share one unblock\n384:### Demoted on inspection\n392:## Re-ranked 2026-09-21, after a sweep of every project\n413:## Corrections to the 2026-09-19 chat answer\n  566 docs/STATUS.md\n  423 docs/JEV_CAPABILITY_MAP.md\n   39 drive_triage/README.md\n 1028 total","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"5de19c84-7b44-48a9-ad50-5824d07a363d","timestamp":"2026-09-28T13:02:50.316Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"1:# STATUS\n5:## Current state\n6:- **2026-09-26 (Drive triage, REGISTERED, not run)**: tenth measurement. Can Jev place the Drive files Flint's keyword rules miss (3,548 of 9,712) into the Zotero taxonomy? Pre-registered in `docs/DRIVE_TRIAGE_PREREG.md` with the 200-file sample (`drive_triage/sample.csv`, seed 20260926). Bars were approved by Eric before any call: confident on at least 60%, domain accuracy at least 90% on the confident answers, and at least equal to Haiku. Next: build the state, then Claude's blind answer key, committed before the first Jev call. Consumer: `erash11/Flint`.\n17:- **2026-09-22 (spring exit notes → trajectory, CLOSED)**: **FAILS by 0.002, the ninth\n365:## Next\n419:## Open questions\n474:## Gotchas\n====\n1:# Jev capability map\n7:## Jev in one screen\n39:## Limits and failure modes\n78:## Where it fits what we run\n101:### PP_Recruiting: not now, and what would change that\n149:## What this unlocks that we cannot do today\n204:## Where not to use it\n221:## Sequence\n245:## Re-ranked 2026-09-20, after five items were resolved\n252:### The rule this project earned, stated as a gate rather than a story\n273:### Answer-key audit: a required step in every pre-registered test (added 2026-09-26)\n298:### Next three\n368:### Blocked on access, not on effort — and both share one unblock\n384:### Demoted on inspection\n392:## Re-ranked 2026-09-21, after a sweep of every project\n413:## Corrections to the 2026-09-19 chat answer\n  566 docs/STATUS.md\n  423 docs/JEV_CAPABILITY_MAP.md\n   39 drive_triage/README.md\n 1028 total","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"5a16392e-89f7-40e8-94e3-8a2dcc7846dc","session_id":"e054b45d-33cd-4562-af51-7c3370696c58","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\TypeSafe_Sandbox\\.claude\\worktrees\\drive-triage-run","sessionId":"e054b45d-33cd-4562-af51-7c3370696c58","version":"2.1.283","gitBranch":"worktree-drive-triage-run"}
