{"parentUuid":"8c465add-13c7-421f-94e8-1eb2dc50184f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfVt9gZQCXx5GqVdeNFGP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XvtW7XemdhvKZq3uxy8zfr","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd \"/c/Users/eric_rash/Desktop/DEV/TypeSafe_Sandbox/.claude/worktrees/drive-triage-run\" && sed -n 5,40p docs/STATUS.md; echo ====; sed -n 245,300p docs/JEV_CAPABILITY_MAP.md; echo ====; cat drive_triage/README.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1096,"cache_read_input_tokens":90079,"output_tokens":171,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1096,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":171,"cache_read_input_tokens":90079,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1096,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1096},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01XvtW7XemdhvKZq3uxy8zfr":{"command":"cd \"/c/Users/eric_rash/Desktop/DEV/TypeSafe_Sandbox/.claude/worktrees/drive-triage-run\" && sed -n 5,40p docs/STATUS.md; echo ====; sed -n 245,300p docs/JEV_CAPABILITY_MAP.md; echo ====; cat drive_triage/README.md"}},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfVt9g68LuahWYogLUc6H","type":"assistant","uuid":"1568f3c3-fd69-4712-a947-e6441784ebd7","timestamp":"2026-09-28T13:02:53.002Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"e054b45d-33cd-4562-af51-7c3370696c58","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\TypeSafe_Sandbox\\.claude\\worktrees\\drive-triage-run","sessionId":"e054b45d-33cd-4562-af51-7c3370696c58","version":"2.1.283","gitBranch":"worktree-drive-triage-run"}
{"parentUuid":"1568f3c3-fd69-4712-a947-e6441784ebd7","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_non_blocking_error","hookName":"PreToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_01XvtW7XemdhvKZq3uxy8zfr","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","stderr":"Failed with non-blocking status code: /usr/bin/bash: line 1: /Users/kristinarash/.local/bin/dcg: No such file or directory","stdout":"","exitCode":127,"command":"/Users/kristinarash/.local/bin/dcg","durationMs":610},"type":"attachment","uuid":"38b470b7-2d75-4abc-a0ed-640a4d385136","timestamp":"2026-09-28T13:02:53.999Z","session_id":"e054b45d-33cd-4562-af51-7c3370696c58","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\TypeSafe_Sandbox\\.claude\\worktrees\\drive-triage-run","sessionId":"e054b45d-33cd-4562-af51-7c3370696c58","version":"2.1.283","gitBranch":"worktree-drive-triage-run"}
{"parentUuid":"1568f3c3-fd69-4712-a947-e6441784ebd7","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"dbbe448b-2aa0-440f-9a91-c30d37d9de00","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XvtW7XemdhvKZq3uxy8zfr","type":"tool_result","content":"## Current state\n- **2026-09-26 (Drive triage, REGISTERED, not run)**: tenth measurement. Can Jev place the Drive files Flint's keyword rules miss (3,548 of 9,712) into the Zotero taxonomy? Pre-registered in `docs/DRIVE_TRIAGE_PREREG.md` with the 200-file sample (`drive_triage/sample.csv`, seed 20260926). Bars were approved by Eric before any call: confident on at least 60%, domain accuracy at least 90% on the confident answers, and at least equal to Haiku. Next: build the state, then Claude's blind answer key, committed before the first Jev call. Consumer: `erash11/Flint`.\n- **2026-09-26 (answer-key audit step)**: added to `docs/JEV_CAPABILITY_MAP.md` as a\n  required step in every pre-registered test: Eric blind-judges Jev's confident\n  disagreements with the labels (max 20), and both scores are reported. The original\n  labels still decide pass or fail. Prompted by the \"Just Ask Jev\" paper (arXiv\n  2609.29429), which found label defects in 3 benchmarks, as we did in 3 write-ups.\n  The rest of that paper (give Jev the source, calibrate thresholds, act only on\n  confident answers) was already practice here. Open, Eric's call: a pre-registered\n  test of Jev checking course summaries against their transcripts, only if someone\n  other than Eric reads those summaries.\n- **2026-09-22 (doctor-plus cleanup)**: Router test fixed. Sports scores now route to `pp-espn` (#27), and ALL CHECKS PASSED. CreateSkill was dropped from the expected-skill lists and the roster rebuilt and installed (127 skills). The Mac still needs `build_roster.py` then `install.py`. The four old worktrees were removed. 8 gitignored `private/` files that existed only in them (fireflies/notes/spring probe sheets and Jev runs) were saved into the main checkout.\n- **2026-09-22 (spring exit notes → trajectory, CLOSED)**: **FAILS by 0.002, the ninth\n  item measured off the map.** Pre-registered in `93c4120` (weights, cut points and\n  both bars fixed before the first call). Composite of four department Scores vs\n  blended snaps: **rho 0.298** against a **0.30** bar (n 34, p 0.087); Claude pass\n  0.352, keyword rubric 0.218. **Stability rho 0.998** over two runs of all 99 (bar\n  0.95), 96/99 same bin, 0 failures. At n=34 the CI is about ±0.33, so 0.298 and 0.352\n  cannot be separated, but a near-miss is still a miss and the bar was not moved. The\n  Claude pass stays and `coach_pdf.py` is untouched. **The finding worth keeping is\n  role, not trajectory:** the held-out role Score hits **rho 0.643** (n 34), and the\n  assumption that role is just extraction is wrong, and was checked — only 5 of 99\n  notes carry a literal \"Role =\", and role words anywhere in the coach note settle\n  16/34 at rho 0.405 (n.s.) where Jev reaches 0.664 on the same 16. That is post-hoc on\n  the same athletes, so it earns **its own pre-registered test against 2026 snaps**\n  once a fresh `pff.db` lands, not a retroactive pass. Write-up:\n  `docs/SPRING_NOTES_TRAJECTORY.md`.\n- **2026-09-22 (Fireflies meeting → project, BUILT and SHIPPED)**: the **first item to\n  pass its pre-registered test** after seven kills. Blind on 40 meetings, Jev was\n  confident on 36/39 and right on 33/36 (bars 60% and 90%); the keyword baseline was\n  right on 1 of 12. **The pass rests mostly on \"none of these\" (27/28).** On real\n  project meetings it was **7 of 11**, and OKRs_2026-27 was the repeat miss (its\n  portfolio purpose is one line). Shipped as `meeting-sync` step 4\n  (`scripts/tag_project.py`) with `meeting-prep` reading the tag: **claude-skills PR #1\n  MERGED** (`2da77af`) and pulled live on Windows; **the Mac needs `git pull` in\n  `~/.claude/skills`**. Backfill over the vault the same day: 246 notes marked, **14\n====\n## Re-ranked 2026-09-20, after five items were resolved\n\nAll three of the original sequence shipped. Five of fourteen rows are now closed:\n`skill_suggestion` (live), `classification_using_confidence` (1,418 records),\n`citation_check` (live and gating, 6 of 6 after the apparatus strip),\n`entity_alignment` (**withdrawn**, measured) and PP_Recruiting screening (**rejected**).\n\n### The rule this project earned, stated as a gate rather than a story\n\nEvery item that was measured moved, and every one moved *down*. Entity alignment was\nranked second and was withdrawn. PP_Recruiting offered two obvious fits that both\ncollapsed into code. The Zotero renames were recommended skip. `AUTO_ACCEPT` came in\nat the cookbook's 0.90 and measured to 0.80; the Zotero cutoff came in at 0.90 and\nmeasured to 0.50. That is not bad luck, it is a missing gate. **Build only where all\nthree hold:**\n\n1. **The answer is genuinely fuzzy** — not a join, not a threshold, not a lookup.\n2. **Something already consumes the answer.** No consumer, no build. This is the\n   Zotero-renames test.\n3. **A code baseline was measured first.** If deterministic code gets most of the way,\n   the model is decoration.\n\nEach withdrawn item failed a *different* one of these, which is why no single check\nwould have caught them. Entity alignment failed (1) — exact string equality settled\n287 of 300 and fuzzy matching contributed zero settled pairs. The Zotero renames\nfailed (2). The prose-number work nearly failed (3) and was saved only because the\nband was measured before and after.\n\n### Answer-key audit: a required step in every pre-registered test (added 2026-09-26)\n\nThree measurements found a bad answer key, not a bad model: the surgery count (17 by\nregex, 22 under blind labels), the Evidence Library tags (the reviewed labels sided\nwith Jev on 5 of 8 rules-picks), and the spring notes (role words the labels missed).\nThe \"Just Ask Jev\" paper (arXiv 2609.29429) reports the same on three public\nbenchmarks. So every pre-registration now carries this step, written down before the\nfirst call:\n\n1. **Pull the confident disagreements.** Every item where Jev's probability clears the\n   pre-registered confidence cut and its answer differs from the label. Fix the cut\n   in the pre-registration, not after seeing results.\n2. **Eric judges them blind.** Shuffle, hide which side said what, show only the input\n   and the two answers. He marks label right, Jev right, or unclear.\n3. **Report both scores.** The pre-registered score on the original labels decides\n   pass or fail, and the bar never moves. The audited score is reported next to it,\n   and the count of labels changed is a finding in its own right.\n4. **Cap the audit.** At most 20 items. If there are more than 20 confident\n   disagreements, audit a random 20 and report the rate. More than that is a label\n   problem worth its own write-up.\n\nWhat this is not: a way to rescue a failed test. A test that fails on the original\nlabels and passes on the audited ones is reported as FAIL, with the audit as the reason\nto re-run against fresh labels.\n\n### Next three\n\n> **ANSWERED 2026-09-20 — `sde_cascade` is a CODE LINTER, not a Jev build.** The\n====\n# Drive triage: the Jev pilot (run record)\n\nPre-registration: `docs/DRIVE_TRIAGE_PREREG.md` (bars fixed 2026-09-26, before any call).\nSample: `sample.csv` (200 files, seed 20260926).\n\n## Order of work (each step committed before the next)\n\n1. `build_state.py`: state for all 200, built by code. Written to `private/state.jsonl`\n   (gitignored: first-page text of Drive documents).\n   **state.jsonl sha256 `779d3ff481960373070214bda7bdfa4079abd68fed20a7f57a3956c99c06aada`**\n2. `answer_key.csv`: Claude's labels (topic, derived domain, route) for all 200. They were written by one\n   fresh agent that read only `private/state.jsonl` and `taxonomy_for_key.md`. It saw no Flint\n   label, no `sample.csv` column beyond what the state carries, and no model answer.\n   It was committed and pushed before the first Jev call.\n3. `run_jev.py`: Jev, one request per file (topic Choice unchanged from `classify.question()`\n   plus the route Choice defined in the script). Raw answers in `runs/jev.jsonl`.\n4. Comparators (Haiku, Codex) and scoring against the bars.\n\n## State as built (2026-09-28)\n\n| Extraction | Files |\n|---|---:|\n| First page (median about 1,870 characters) | 113 |\n| Path and name only (video, audio, data files; by design) | 53 |\n| PDF with no text layer (scans) | 18 |\n| Empty in Drive (size 0; the Drive entry holds no content) | 7 |\n| Not a readable PDF (3 macOS `._` resource forks, 1 damaged file) | 4 |\n| Legacy Office format (.doc, .ppt) | 3 |\n| Encrypted PDF | 1 |\n| PDF parser limit | 1 |\n\nSo 87 of 200 files carry no first-page text. That is thinner than the pre-registration\nassumed, but identical for every model and for the answer key.\n\nMethod notes:\n- All documents were fetched by Drive id with `gws`, one method for every root.\n- There is no Anthropic API key on this machine. Haiku runs through headless\n  `claude -p --model claude-haiku-4-5`, one call per file with the same state and the same\n  forced topic.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"644f6b77-dc99-4bd7-b3ff-ef604fb4a9e2","timestamp":"2026-09-28T13:03:08.041Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"## Current state\n- **2026-09-26 (Drive triage, REGISTERED, not run)**: tenth measurement. Can Jev place the Drive files Flint's keyword rules miss (3,548 of 9,712) into the Zotero taxonomy? Pre-registered in `docs/DRIVE_TRIAGE_PREREG.md` with the 200-file sample (`drive_triage/sample.csv`, seed 20260926). Bars were approved by Eric before any call: confident on at least 60%, domain accuracy at least 90% on the confident answers, and at least equal to Haiku. Next: build the state, then Claude's blind answer key, committed before the first Jev call. Consumer: `erash11/Flint`.\n- **2026-09-26 (answer-key audit step)**: added to `docs/JEV_CAPABILITY_MAP.md` as a\n  required step in every pre-registered test: Eric blind-judges Jev's confident\n  disagreements with the labels (max 20), and both scores are reported. The original\n  labels still decide pass or fail. Prompted by the \"Just Ask Jev\" paper (arXiv\n  2609.29429), which found label defects in 3 benchmarks, as we did in 3 write-ups.\n  The rest of that paper (give Jev the source, calibrate thresholds, act only on\n  confident answers) was already practice here. Open, Eric's call: a pre-registered\n  test of Jev checking course summaries against their transcripts, only if someone\n  other than Eric reads those summaries.\n- **2026-09-22 (doctor-plus cleanup)**: Router test fixed. Sports scores now route to `pp-espn` (#27), and ALL CHECKS PASSED. CreateSkill was dropped from the expected-skill lists and the roster rebuilt and installed (127 skills). The Mac still needs `build_roster.py` then `install.py`. The four old worktrees were removed. 8 gitignored `private/` files that existed only in them (fireflies/notes/spring probe sheets and Jev runs) were saved into the main checkout.\n- **2026-09-22 (spring exit notes → trajectory, CLOSED)**: **FAILS by 0.002, the ninth\n  item measured off the map.** Pre-registered in `93c4120` (weights, cut points and\n  both bars fixed before the first call). Composite of four department Scores vs\n  blended snaps: **rho 0.298** against a **0.30** bar (n 34, p 0.087); Claude pass\n  0.352, keyword rubric 0.218. **Stability rho 0.998** over two runs of all 99 (bar\n  0.95), 96/99 same bin, 0 failures. At n=34 the CI is about ±0.33, so 0.298 and 0.352\n  cannot be separated, but a near-miss is still a miss and the bar was not moved. The\n  Claude pass stays and `coach_pdf.py` is untouched. **The finding worth keeping is\n  role, not trajectory:** the held-out role Score hits **rho 0.643** (n 34), and the\n  assumption that role is just extraction is wrong, and was checked — only 5 of 99\n  notes carry a literal \"Role =\"