{"parentUuid":"c4cecf9e-5eaf-4ff1-a58e-9a6e507acb82","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfVvGw4xrN4UZ6coJqQ8S","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Claude Code stopped both comparator runs because the machine ran low on memory. I haven't restarted them, since that needs your OK. What finished before the stop is committed and pushed as `eb73f14` on `worktree-drive-triage-run`.\n\n| Run | Answers saved | Left |\n|---|---|---|\n| Jev | 200/200 | done |\n| Haiku | 181/200 | 19 (about 15 minutes) |\n| Codex | 23/200 | 177 (about 2.7 hours at ~55s each) |\n\n- **Codex works.** Its command had never been tried before; a 2-file test passed with no errors, so the full run just needs time.\n- **Nothing is scored yet.** The Jev-versus-Haiku bar only counts once Haiku has all 200 answers. Jev already fails the 90% accuracy bar (76.5%), so the verdict stays FAIL either way. The Haiku result decides which comparator does Flint's pass.\n- **The cause is memory.** Right now about 0.9 GB is free with 23 Claude processes open. Running Haiku and Codex side by side was more than the machine could hold, and that was my call.\n\n**Next:** close some Claude sessions, then tell me to go. I'll finish Haiku first on its own (about 15 minutes), then score and write up the result. Codex runs after that and fills in its row when it finishes. Both runs pick up where they stopped."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":466,"cache_read_input_tokens":100655,"output_tokens":571,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":107},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":466,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":571,"cache_read_input_tokens":100655,"cache_creation_input