{"parentUuid":"7418e7e5-85c4-433f-931a-086eb0b4d058","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfVvWPLPVZiipyC9ncYd8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You don't have 20 sessions open. That count was wrong, and I passed it on without checking. Only **3 are real Claude Code sessions**. The rest of the \"claude\" processes are helper pieces of the Claude desktop app, which shows up as about 15 processes.\n\nWhat's actually using your memory (15.6 GB total, 0.4 GB free):\n\n| What | Memory | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| **memsearch reindex** (started 8:26 AM) | **2.5 GB** | This is the big one. It's the memory search index rebuilding, started by the memory tooling. It should finish and exit on its own. |\n| Claude desktop app (all its helpers together) | ~0.6 GB | Close the app window if you're not using it. |\n| This session | ~0.3 GB | Needed for the pilot. |\n| An older background session from **Sep 26, 6:47 PM** | ~0.2 GB | Probably finished work that's still sitting idle. |\n| Your terminal Claude session (started 7:56 AM) | ~0.1 GB | Probably the one you're typing in. |\n| Chrome, Edge, WebView | ~1.5 GB | Closing tabs helps a bit. |\n\n**What to do:**\n1. **Let the memsearch reindex finish.** Killing it mid-run can leave the index half-built. It frees 2.5 GB when it exits.\n2. **Close the Claude desktop app** if you aren't using it right now: quit it from the system tray icon, not just the window.\n3. **The Sep 26 background session:** type `/tasks` or `/bg` in your terminal Claude to see background jobs and stop it. I'm not certain which of those two commands this version has. Or tell me to, and I'll stop that one process (PID 78920) for you.\n\nWhen memsearch is done and free memory is above about 2 GB, say \"go\". I'll run Haiku's last 19 files, then score and write up the result."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_c