{"parentUuid":"59341127-e82c-4b8a-8046-edf6199ba608","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfW331X2jykTNquBfSf1g","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Loaded. Yesterday's plan was the **Flint method interview**: the 27 questions in `Flint/docs/interview-prep.md` plus the 6 peaking questions from the peaking synthesis. Every synthesis note is blocked on \"where Eric lands,\" and these answers fill that in.\n\n**How this runs:**\n- Three questions overlap, so they're merged, which leaves **30 questions in 5 rounds of about 6**, most important first.\n- Short answers are fine. \"Skip\", \"not mine\", \"don't know\" and \"legacy\" are all useful answers.\n- I record your answers **in your words**, into Flint as the source of truth for the baseline.\n\nHaiku keeps running in the background. I'll mention it only if it needs you.\n\n---\n\n### Round 1 of 5: the load-bearing ones\n\n**1. Course material: which positions are yours?** HHPR 5355 is co-taught with Chris Ruf and Mike Wenger. Of these, which do you personally hold, and which are shared course material?\n- (a) the Vermeil hierarchy as your compass\n- (b) undulating over linear periodization, and is it still your default? Where do you deviate?\n- (c) Dynamic Correspondence\n- (d) the energy-system priority stack for football\n\n**2. mRSI readiness rule.** You replaced wellness surveys with force-plate mRSI. What drop, on which day of the week, actually changes the plan? Do linemen and low-snap players get their own thresholds?\n\n**3. Retiring a test.** You dropped roster-wide NordBord (time cost, staff turnover) and daily wellness surveys (athletes gamed them). Is there a general rule for the next tech or protocol decision, or is each one a fresh call?\n\n**4. Return to play.** The Playbook says Applied Performance *supports* Athletic Medicine's RTP decisions.\n- What criteria, battery or sign-off do you actually contribute, and where does your input end?\n- Is there any written phased RTP protocol, even an informal one, or is it built case by case?\n\n**5. Department model.** Is Applied Performance a peer discipline that enables Athletic Performance, Athletic Medicine and Nutrition, or in-house programming support for the Athletic Performance staff? Or both, depending on the situation?\n\n**6. Coach's eye versus objective data.** The course says a good coach's eye beats a fancy test, and warns that monitoring culture breeds fear-driven under-training. Your own writing replaced subjective self-report with an objective number. Where do you draw the line?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4722,"cache_read_input_tokens":147202,"output_tokens":1348,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":516},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4722,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1348,"cache_read_input_tokens":147202,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4722,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4722},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfW3315ju3P5dZwhufJA9","attributionSkill":"interview-me","type":"assistant","uuid":"f4b22ece-674f-4cc6-9521-6a052a0df021","timestamp":"2026-09-28T14:59:34.616Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"e054b45d-33cd-4562-af51-7c3370696c58","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\TypeSafe_Sandbox\\.claude\\worktrees\\drive-triage-run","sessionId":"e054b45d-33cd-4562-af51-7c3370696c58","version":"2.1.283","gitBranch":"worktree-drive-triage-run"}
