{"parentUuid":"d7c90648-dee1-46a5-96ed-019a37e87654","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfW3PuPmJidZKLNCAXnBb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":51,"cache_read_input_tokens":156003,"output_tokens":953,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":253},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":51,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":953,"cache_read_input_tokens":156003,"cache_creation_input_tokens":51,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":51},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfW3Ptes3AGfwnDjaKNux","type":"assistant","uuid":"9249f5e6-1e2f-441c-b007-56111fe11da6","timestamp":"2026-09-28T15:04:07.030Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"e054b45d-33cd-4562-af51-7c3370696c58","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\TypeSafe_Sandbox\\.claude\\worktrees\\drive-triage-run","sessionId":"e054b45d-33cd-4562-af51-7c3370696c58","version":"2.1.283","gitBranch":"worktree-drive-triage-run"}
{"parentUuid":"9249f5e6-1e2f-441c-b007-56111fe11da6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfW3PuPmJidZKLNCAXnBb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Recorded: **Jev does the Flint pass**, since it beats Haiku. The pilot is still written up as a FAIL on the 90% bar, with this as your decision on top of it. Going in, remember that about **1 in 4 of Jev's confident answers had the wrong domain.** So Flint's shortlists should keep your approval step and not trust Jev's domain blindly. If Codex beats Jev when it finishes, I'll tell you.\n\n---\n\n### Round 1 of 5: the load-bearing ones\n\nShort answers are fine, and \"skip\", \"not mine\" or \"legacy\" count as answers.\n\n**1. Course material: which positions are yours?** HHPR 5355 is co-taught with Chris Ruf and Mike Wenger. Of these, which do you personally hold, and which are shared course material?\n- (a) the Vermeil hierarchy as your compass\n- (b) undulating over linear periodization, and is it still your default? Where do you deviate?\n- (c) Dynamic Correspondence\n- (d) the energy-system priority stack for football\n\n**2. mRSI readiness rule.** What mRSI drop, on which day of the week, actually changes the plan? Do linemen and low-snap players get their own thresholds?\n\n**3. Retiring a test.** You dropped roster-wide NordBord (time cost, staff turnover) and daily wellness surveys (athletes gamed them). Is there a general rule for the next tech or protocol decision, or is each one a fresh call?\n\n**4. Return to play.**\n- What criteria, battery or sign-off do you contribute to Athletic Medicine's RTP decisions, and where does your input end?\n- Is there any written phased RTP protocol, even an informal one?\n\n**5. Department model.** Is Applied Performance a peer discipline that enables Athletic Performance, Athletic Medicine and Nutrition, or in-house programming support for the Athletic Performance staff? Or both?\n\n**6. Coach's eye versus objective data.** The course says a good coach's eye beats a fancy test. Your own writing replaced subjective self-report with an objective force-plate number. Where do you draw the line?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":51,"cache_read_input_tokens":156003,"output_tokens":953,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":253},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":51,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":953,"cache_read_input_tokens":156003,"cache_creation_input_tokens":51,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":51},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfW3Ptes3AGfwnDjaKNux","type":"assistant","uuid":"26a81d6a-6e39-4e6b-9694-8537e961d99f","timestamp":"2026-09-28T15:04:12.290Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"e054b45d-33cd-4562-af51-7c3370696c58","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\TypeSafe_Sandbox\\.claude\\worktrees\\drive-triage-run","sessionId":"e054b45d-33cd-4562-af51-7c3370696c58","version":"2.1.283","gitBranch":"worktree-drive-triage-run"}
