{"parentUuid":"a45215f0-d12b-415f-af8e-5d53680ba3d1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfW7mNfeHKYjEyFVyP8NP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Mxu3Cy9gEWSfWQZxvDfNcc","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\Flint\\.claude\\worktrees\\step1-triage\\docs\\interview\\2026-09-28-method-interview.md","content":"---\ndate: 2026-09-28\nsource: live /interview-me session (Claude Code)\nquestions: docs/interview-prep.md (27) + docs/synthesis/peaking-and-taper-in-season-football.md §8 (6); overlaps merged\nstatus: in progress\n---\n\n# Flint method interview, 2026-09-28\n\nEric's answers, in his words (typos fixed only). Each answer turns the matching\n`method-baseline.md` position from Inferred to Explicit, or records what he said instead.\n\n## Round 1: the load-bearing ones\n\n**1. Course material (HHPR 5355): which positions are yours?** Vermeil hierarchy as compass;\nundulating over linear periodization; Dynamic Correspondence; the football energy-system\npriority stack.\n> All of them.\n\n**2. mRSI readiness rule** (also peaking Q5). Which drop, on which day, changes the plan?\nSeparate thresholds for linemen and low-snap players?\n> Wednesdays, the thresholds should be individualized.\n\n**3. Retiring a test or technology.** General rule, or a fresh call each time?\n> If it doesn't answer a question anyone has, or a direct need, then it doesn't have a place.\n\n**4. Return to play.** What Applied Performance contributes, where its input ends; is there a\nwritten phased protocol?\n> Testing and progression. I collaborate on loading and progression decisions when needed.\n> It doesn't really end. There is a written protocol, I can provide it.\n\n**5. Department model.** Peer discipline enabling Athletic Performance, Athletic Medicine and\nNutrition, or in-house programming support for Athletic Performance?\n> Both.\n\n**6. Coach's eye versus objective data.** Where is the line?\n> There is a place for the coach's eye: when something looks off, it can direct you where to\n> look and gather data to investigate further.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":535,"cache_read_input_tokens":162472,"output_tokens":737,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":535,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":737,"cache_read_input_tokens":162472,"cache_creation_input_tokens":535,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":535},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Mxu3Cy9gEWSfWQZxvDfNcc":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\Flint\\.claude\\worktrees\\step1-triage\\docs\\interview\\2026-09-28-method-interview.md","content":"---\ndate: 2026-09-28\nsource: live /interview-me session (Claude Code)\nquestions: docs/interview-prep.md (27) + docs/synthesis/peaking-and-taper-in-season-football.md §8 (6); overlaps merged\nstatus: in progress\n---\n\n# Flint method interview, 2026-09-28\n\nEric's answers, in his words (typos fixed only). Each answer turns the matching\n`method-baseline.md` position from Inferred to Explicit, or records what he said instead.\n\n## Round 1: the load-bearing ones\n\n**1. Course material (HHPR 5355): which positions are yours?** Vermeil hierarchy as compass;\nundulating over linear periodization; Dynamic Correspondence; the football energy-system\npriority stack.\n> All of them.\n\n**2. mRSI readiness rule** (also peaking Q5). Which drop, on which day, changes the plan?\nSeparate thresholds for linemen and low-snap players?\n> Wednesdays, the thresholds should be individualized.\n\n**3. Retiring a test or technology.** General rule, or a fresh call each time?\n> If it doesn't answer a question anyone has, or a direct need, then it doesn't have a place.\n\n**4. Return to play.** What Applied Performance contributes, where its input ends; is there a\nwritten phased protocol?\n> Testing and progression. I collaborate on loading and progression decisions when needed.\n> It doesn't really end. There is a written protocol, I can provide it.\n\n**5. Department model.** Peer discipline enabling Athletic Performance, Athletic Medicine and\nNutrition, or in-house programming support for Athletic Performance?\n> Both.\n\n**6. Coach's eye versus objective data.** Where is the line?\n> There is a place for the coach's eye: when something looks off, it can direct you where to\n> look and gather data to investigate further.\n"}},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfW7mNDrbJy3JLiPVC8NQ","type":"assistant","uuid":"10f68be6-2254-41db-b385-b9bf9e549aa8","timestamp":"2026-09-28T16:01:27.189Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"e054b45d-33cd-4562-af51-7c3370696c58","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\Flint\\.claude\\worktrees\\step1-triage","sessionId":"e054b45d-33cd-4562-af51-7c3370696c58","version":"2.1.283","gitBranch":"step1-triage"}
