{"parentUuid":"d78e9512-557d-4953-956c-e56d50fcb56f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfW7mqRUJMkgMcQcgNHTh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Round 1 is saved to `Flint/docs/interview/2026-09-28-method-interview.md`.\n\nTwo quick follow-ups on Round 1. Answer them with Round 2 if you like:\n- **2a.** \"Individualized\" against what: each player's typical error, a percent drop from their own baseline, or something else?\n- **4a.** Where does the written RTP protocol live? A file path or name is enough and I'll pull it in.\n\n---\n\n### Round 2 of 5: testing, force plate, load\n\n**7. GPS and load thresholds per sport.** Your gap analysis says none are documented. Do any exist informally?\n\n**8. Assessment Manual V12.** Is it current, partly replaced, or legacy?\n- It references GymAware and a contact-mat CMJ, while the current setup is Perch and ForceDecks.\n- It says \"don't coach the jump strategy\", but Force Plate Testing V3 gives cues (\"chest up\", \"land softly\"). Which instruction holds?\n\n**9. Testing cadence.** How often does each sport test now? Has that changed since the V4 Assessment Table?\n\n**10. From rep-max to true 1RM.** What training-age or experience marker moves an athlete from rep-max testing to true 1RM testing?\n\n**11. System of record.** When Kitman Labs and VALD Hub or OpenField disagree on a number, which one wins?\n\n**12. Injury-risk model.** Do you use ACWR or any formal risk model, or deliberately avoid them? In a movement screen (Fusionetics or similar), what finding actually changes a program, versus just being logged?\n\n**13. Change of direction.** COD is in the V4 table for several sports, but no protocol exists anywhere. What do you actually use?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":849,"cache_read_input_tokens":163007,"output_tokens":567,"output_tok