{"parentUuid":"84876cce-a37e-4557-af15-1c2250bc9842","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"SessionStart:resume","toolUseID":"69298d17-10a3-4efc-9626-c6db286113f2","hookEvent":"SessionStart","content":"","stdout":"{\"hookSpecificOutput\":{\"hookEventName\":\"SessionStart\",\"additionalContext\":\"## User profile (global-memory/USER.md)\\n\\n<!-- Cap: 1,375 chars. Updated when the agent learns durable user preferences. -->\\r\\n# User Profile\\r\\n\\r\\n## About\\r\\nEric Rash, Director of Applied Performance, Baylor Athletics. Builds football GPS and force-plate pipelines. Wife Kristina; kids Ames, Saylor, Rowan (5, 4, 10mo on 2026-09-01). Career target: analytics-first player-coach near Iowa, $90K+ floor, mid-2027. Read `~/DEV/ContextVault` before career or personal advice.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Preferences\\r\\n- Python/R. macOS primary since 2026-08-05; Windows 11 still active. Tool paths: CLAUDE.md.\\r\\n- Local SQLite/DuckDB. No cloud servers or schedulers without Baylor IT approval. Google Drive only; keep DuckDB local to avoid sync locks.\\r\\n- Tangible working examples over documentation.\\r\\n- Staff-facing text: Athletic Performance (not S&C), Athletic Medicine (not sports medicine), Applied Performance (not sport science).\\r\\n\\r\\n## Working Style\\r\\n- Direct; says \\\"stop\\\" when done. Challenge vague or rehearsed reasoning: \\\"sharpened, not soothed.\\\"\\r\\n- Decide standard technical details, state the choice, and move on.\\r\\n- Build in small steps. Do not break mid-season work.\\r\\n- Authors direction when leadership does not; OKR-driven change agent in a status-quo group.\\r\\n- Right question over downstream craft; Christian faith is his organizing frame.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Working memory (global-memory/MEMORY.md)\\n\\n<!-- Cap: 2,500 chars. Working scratchpad; writes take effect next session. -->\\r\\n# Working Memory\\r\\n\\r\\n## Active Threads\\r\\n- **Prioritization slate (9/14)**: LIVE, 5/5. →Tier A prioritization-slate\\r\\n- **Status report**: #3 by 9/25, biweekly to 12/18. →Tier A supervisor-log-pipeline\\r\\n- **Personal site (9/2)**: phone check; host or local? →Tier A personal-site-build-routes\\r\\n- **RTP CLA (9/26)**: L1–2 + Sprint Film Check built. NEXT: Tim/Jacob → export; Joe notes → L3. →`RTP_Constraints_Course/docs/`\\r\\n- **ATH Tech**: shipped; ITS pending; run 9/29. →Tier A tech-inventory-refresh\\r\\n- **Machine split (9/24)**: Win=day, Mac=eve; Mac sole writer GPS/Perch/VALD. →handoff 2026-09-24-machine-split\\r\\n- **Ship queue (9/25)**: K-B self-audit done. Ship to a named user q2wk: RI5 #002 (`_v2` only) wk 9/28, intern M1 10/9, AP Digest ch1 10/23. →`RunningTheRoom/docs/STATUS.md`\\r\\n- **FB matchups (9/23)**: EPA = PFF via `scripts/pff_epa_profile.py`. Wk4 COLO: EPA layer only, full profile? →`MatchupAnalysis_FB2026/docs/`\\r\\n- **PP Recruiting (9/26)**: 013 built; size Q + 011 await Mauro (asst GM). →`PP_Recruiting/docs/`\\r\\n- **Sleep sched (9/16)**: R1 merged; NEXT night/early-kickoff. →`sleep-scheduler/`\\r\\n- **TypeSafe (9/26)**: gate log-only, review ~10/6; Drive-triage prereg #30. NEXT: Y/Ns 22 surgeries. →`TypeSafe_Sandbox/docs/`\\r\\n- **Flint (9/26)**: sport-sci KB, side lane. Harries in vault; 7 staged, fixes pending. →`Flint/docs/STATUS.md`\\n- **PFF DB (9/22)**: swap Parquet on Drive, never the DB. Both: 2026 thru wk3 + video. →`PFF_Data_Project/docs/`\\r\\n\\r\\n## Environment Notes\\r\\n- Hooks: patch both copies only for shared events; Codex has no prompt-submit event. →Tier A hook-two-copies-trap.\\r\\n- daily-backup: manifest entries alone copy nothing; sweep nested ~/.claude repos →handoff 09-19.\\r\\n- `DEV/Linda Projects` = private I-983 repo; folder has a space, repo an underscore.\\r\\n- `~/DEV` = THIN repo; `.gitignore` starts `/*` — never remove. →Tier A github-consolidation.\\r\\n- Win: `Desktop\\\\DEV` syncs via Drive (robocopy retired 9/22). No large DBs/junctions: renv via `RENV_PATHS_LIBRARY_ROOT`, PFF via `PFF_DB`.\\r\\n- Schedules →automation-cadence. CFB capture Mac only. Dashboard →command-centre.\\n- Post-merge: delete merged branches/worktrees unasked (verify first) →Tier A post-merge-cleanup.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Pending Decisions\\r\\n- **OKR gate (9/14)**: AI buy-in + data governance (Anthony = outside-firm adviser, NOT Mauro). NCAA charter or park?\\n\\n---\\n\\n## HOOK FAILURES — surface these to the user on the first response\\n\\n[2026-09-28T00:05:00.821Z] memsearch-sync: index ETIMEDOUT 6x consecutively — indexing may not be keeping up: spawnSync memsearch ETIMEDOUT\\r\\n[2026-09-28T00:15:05.694Z] memsearch-sync: index ETIMEDOUT 7x consecutively — indexing may not be keeping up: spawnSync memsearch ETIMEDOUT\\r\\n[2026-09-28T00:25:11.613Z] memsearch-sync: index ETIMEDOUT 8x consecutively — indexing may not be keeping up: spawnSync memsearch ETIMEDOUT\\r\\n[2026-09-28T00:35:15.559Z] memsearch-sync: index ETIMEDOUT 9x consecutively — indexing may not be keeping up: spawnSync memsearch ETIMEDOUT\\r\\n[2026-09-28T00:45:35.875Z] memsearch-sync: index ETIMEDOUT 10x consecutively — indexing may not be keeping up: spawnSync memsearch ETIMEDOUT\\r\\n[2026-09-28T00:55:48.213Z] memsearch-sync: index ETIMEDOUT 11x consecutively — indexing may not be keeping up: spawnSync memsearch ETIMEDOUT\\r\\n[2026-09-28T01:06:01.376Z] memsearch-sync: index ETIMEDOUT 12x consecutively — indexing may not be keeping up: spawnSync memsearch ETIMEDOUT\\r\\n[2026-09-28T01:07:20.858053+00:00] compiler-stale-lock: reclaimed compile lock held 30min by pid 105800 (compile.py --auto)\\r\\n[2026-09-28T01:16:06.400Z] memsearch-sync: index ETIMEDOUT 13x consecutively — indexing may not be keeping up: spawnSync memsearch ETIMEDOUT\\r\\n[2026-09-28T01:22:17.924034+00:00] compiler-flush-failed: memory-compiler flush failed (session dfcdad2e-ccca-4733-9c03-756f49a6eb04): FLUSH_ERROR: ResultError: Claude Code returned an error result: You've hit your session limit · resets 10:50pm (America/Chicago) (exit code: 1