{"parentUuid":"52c28587-1c67-4ccd-b38b-69a87348ae77","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"UserPromptSubmit","toolUseID":"e4b6c25a-cd47-47cc-ba51-b6ee45e7a740","hookEvent":"UserPromptSubmit","content":"<skill_relevance>\r\nRelevant to the current request: anthropic-skills:docx. Ignore this if it does not fit what the user actually asked for.\r\n</skill_relevance>","stdout":"<skill_relevance>\r\nRelevant to the current request: anthropic-skills:docx. Ignore this if it does not fit what the user actually asked for.\r\n</skill_relevance>\r\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"python3 \"$HOME/.claude/skill-router/router.py\"","durationMs":841},"type":"attachment","uuid":"c744af60-ede6-4635-8ecd-3a80a8ba058f","timestamp":"2026-09-28T17:14:30.814Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nUserPromptSubmit hook success: <skill_relevance>\r\nRelevant to the current request: anthropic-skills:docx. Ignore this if it does not fit what the user actually asked for.\r\n</skill_relevance>\n</system-reminder>"}],"sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\Flint\\.claude\\worktrees\\step1-triage","sessionId":"e054b45d-33cd-4562-af51-7c3370696c58","version":"2.1.283","gitBranch":"step1-triage"}
{"parentUuid":"c744af60-ede6-4635-8ecd-3a80a8ba058f","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"instructions","files":[{"path":"C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\Flint\\.claude\\worktrees\\step1-triage\\CLAUDE.md","type":"Project","content":"@AGENTS.md"},{"path":"C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\Flint\\.claude\\worktrees\\step1-triage\\AGENTS.md","type":"Project","content":"# AGENTS.md\r\n\r\nProject: Flint\r\n\r\n## What this is\r\nFlint is Claude working as Eric's sport-science, performance, S&C and rehab thought\r\npartner. This repo builds the knowledge base behind that role. It catalogs Eric's\r\nDrive (his own material, TB's Training Info, Landon Evans, courses, papers), routes the\r\nhigh-value sources into Zotero and the SecondBrain vault, and writes per-discipline\r\nsynthesis notes that compare the sources against Eric's own method. It is a side-lane\r\nproject, outside the prioritization-slate cap. See `README.md` for the approach and\r\n`docs/PLAN.md` for the checklist.\r\n\r\n## Session routine\r\n- Start: run `git pull`, then read docs/STATUS.md before doing anything else.\r\n- End: update docs/STATUS.md (done, next, open questions), commit, and `git push`.\r\n- Never leave uncommitted work at the end of a session.\r\n\r\n## Conventions\r\n- Durable notes and decisions go in docs/, committed. Not in chat, not in cloud project docs.\r\n- Documents, data exports, and deliverables live on the primary storage drive (Google Drive 00_Primary_Storage_Drive), not in the repo. Files over 95 MB never go in git.\r\n- `data/` is gitignored except aggregate summaries. Regenerate the file-level manifest with `pwsh scripts/build_manifest.ps1`.\r\n- Codex workers read staged copies in `staging/`, never the Drive root. DexaProject, athlete snapshots, Catapult and PFF exports are never catalogued.\r\n- The ingest review gate has two stages.\r\n  1. Before atomizing, verify the source artifact by an independent route: page order, scanned versus text, transcripts checked against captions.\r\n  2. Before promoting, Codex reviews the staged entries against the staged sources, with instructions to falsify (`staging/review_<source>_codex.md`). Nothing reaches the vault without a GO or a GO AFTER FIXES that has been applied.\r\n- Library entries label every voice. The source author's statements are plain. Eric's judgments get \"Eric's review:\". The entry writer's own reasoning gets \"Inference:\". No unlabeled judgments. Every number carries a timestamp or page the reviewer can check, and a claim is only tagged \"confirmed in PDF\" if that PDF is staged. (Learned from the Harries review, 2026-09-26: 25 of 35 files needed fixes, mostly for attribution.)\r\n- Writing: plain, direct, no em dashes. Documents use the Baylor design system."}],"changed":true,"reason":"session_start"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"ed74c362-339c-43be-beae-0e448d3082bd","timestamp":"2026-09-28T17:14:30.915Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nInstruction files were re-read when this session started; these differ from their earlier copies — each replaces its earlier copy, and the instructions preamble above still applies:\n\nContents of C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\Flint\\.claude\\worktrees\\step1-triage\\CLAUDE.md (project instructions, checked into the codebase):\n\n@AGENTS.md\n\nContents of C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\Flint\\.claude\\worktrees\\step1-triage\\AGENTS.md (project instructions, checked into the codebase):\n\n# AGENTS.md\r\n\r\nProject: Flint\r\n\r\n## What this is\r\nFlint is Claude working as Eric's sport-science, performance, S&C and rehab thought\r\npartner. This repo builds the knowledge base behind that role. It catalogs Eric's\r\nDrive (his own material, TB's Training Info, Landon Evans, courses, papers), routes the\r\nhigh-value sources into Zotero and the SecondBrain vault, and writes per-discipline\r\nsynthesis notes that compare the sources against Eric's own method. It is a side-lane\r\nproject, outside the prioritization-slate cap. See `README.md` for the approach and\r\n`docs/PLAN.md` for the checklist.\r\n\r\n## Session routine\r\n- Start: run `git pull`, then read docs/STATUS.md before doing anything else.\r\n- End: update docs/STATUS.md (done, next, open questions), commit, and `git push`.\r\n- Never leave uncommitted work at the end of a session.\r\n\r\n## Conventions\r\n- Durable notes and decisions go in docs/, committed. Not in chat, not in cloud project docs.\r\n- Documents, data exports, and deliverables live on the primary storage drive (Google Drive 00_Primary_Storage_Drive), not in the repo. Files over 95 MB never go in git.\r\n- `data/` is gitignored except aggregate summaries. Regenerate the file-level manifest with `pwsh scripts/build_manifest.ps1`.\r\n- Codex workers read staged copies in `staging/`, never the Drive root. DexaProject, athlete snapshots, Catapult and PFF exports are never catalogued.\r\n- The ingest review gate has two stages.\r\n  1. Before atomizing, verify the source artifact by an independent route: page order, scanned versus text, transcripts checked against captions.\r\n  2. Before promoting, Codex reviews the staged entries against the staged sources, with instructions to falsify (`staging/review_<source>_codex.md`). Nothing reaches the vault without a GO or a GO AFTER FIXES that has been applied.\r\n- Library entries label every voice. The source author's statements are plain. Eric's judgments get \"Eric's review:\". The entry writer's own reasoning gets \"Inference:\". No unlabeled judgments. Every number carries a timestamp or page the reviewer can check, and a claim is only tagged \"confirmed in PDF\" if that PDF is staged. (Learned from the Harries review, 2026-09-26: 25 of 35 files needed fixes, mostly for attribution.)\r\n- Writing: plain, direct, no em dashes. Documents use the Baylor design system.\n</system-reminder>"}],"session_id":"e054b45d-33cd-4562-af51-7c3370696c58","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\Flint\\.claude\\worktrees\\step1-triage","sessionId":"e054b45d-33cd-4562-af51-7c3370696c58","version":"2.1.283","gitBranch":"step1-triage"}
