{"type":"pr-link","sessionId":"e054b45d-33cd-4562-af51-7c3370696c58","prNumber":1,"prUrl":"https://github.com/erash11/Flint/pull/1","prRepository":"erash11/Flint","timestamp":"2026-09-28T17:15:00.049Z"}
{"parentUuid":"18cf84d7-a8d6-4d8c-8088-80684f1e717e","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14989512 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"b052486c-8270-4de7-a9a2-c4a20285296d","timestamp":"2026-09-28T17:14:59.586Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14989512 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"session_id":"e054b45d-33cd-4562-af51-7c3370696c58","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\Flint\\.claude\\worktrees\\step1-triage","sessionId":"e054b45d-33cd-4562-af51-7c3370696c58","version":"2.1.283","gitBranch":"step1-triage"}
{"parentUuid":"b052486c-8270-4de7-a9a2-c4a20285296d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfWDP2BvmeY23zsz87oxR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Round 2 is saved and pushed (`998f597`).\n\n**Two answers change the baseline outright:**\n- **No true 1RM testing, and projected maxes instead.** Several baseline bullets assumed 1RM testing, and they now come out.\n- **The Assessment Manual and the V4 schedule are legacy.** The testing section of the baseline gets relabeled from current practice to legacy.\n\n---\n\n### Round 3 of 5: strength, conditioning, peaking\n\nYour \"Wednesdays\" answer from Round 1 already covers part of question 15.\n\n**14. What does \"peak\" mean in football for you:** every Saturday, target games, or only the postseason? And does the postseason, such as before a bowl, get its own 1 to 3 week taper?\n\n**15. The week after a game.** Issurin's week, shifted for a Saturday game, puts the heavy lifts on Monday and Tuesday, 48 to 72 hours after the game, while fast force is still down. Where do your heaviest lifts and hardest practice sit? Should heavy and high-velocity work wait until Wednesday?\n\n**16. Which quality fades first when it isn't trained?** Your Class 4 slides say aerobic fitness goes first and speed lasts longest. Issurin says the opposite: speed goes in about 5 days, strength and aerobic last about 30. Which do you believe, and does it drive how often you schedule speed work in season?\n\n**17. Bye weeks.** How are they used now: recovery, extra loading, or a speed and strength top-up? Does it differ by position?\n\n**18. In-season strength dose.** Beyond \"keep intensity, cut volume\", what are the actual sets, reps and loads by sport, or at least for football?\n\n**19. Glycolytic conditioning in football.** The course plan says don't program it directly; camp and practice cover it. Has that held up, or do you now program it in some situations?\n\n**20. Anaerobic-threshold heart rate.** Which method do you use: the age-based formula or the body-size table? Both slides sit back to back in Class 4.\n\n**21. The SJ-CMJ gap on ForceDecks.** Do you use it to choose training methods, and in which direction?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":727,"cache_read_input_tokens":174299,"output_tokens":714,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":727,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":714,"cache_read_input_tokens":174299,"cache_creation_input_tokens":727,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":727},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfWDP1kPerA8s7vKwDbJA","type":"assistant","uuid":"1cbf1a60-fa86-4fc4-befd-ab27f508e51a","timestamp":"2026-09-28T17:15:07.165Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"e054b45d-33cd-4562-af51-7c3370696c58","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\Flint\\.claude\\worktrees\\step1-triage","sessionId":"e054b45d-33cd-4562-af51-7c3370696c58","version":"2.1.283","gitBranch":"step1-triage"}
