{"parentUuid":"df5b354b-5269-4730-a75a-5933b4f0c286","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfWFu5oJ2RDw7zoDSXJJ3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YP86fALTmxcG4Rk6brpfQL","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\Flint\\.claude\\worktrees\\step1-triage\\docs\\STATUS.md","old_string":"Read this first. Update it before ending every session.\n","new_string":"Read this first. Update it before ending every session.\n\n## Method interview (2026-09-28): DONE, answers not yet applied\n- Eric answered all 27 interview-prep questions and the 6 peaking questions (merged to 30): `docs/interview/2026-09-28-method-interview.md`, in his words.\n- Its last section lists every change for `method-baseline.md` and the peaking synthesis. Biggest: course positions are Eric's (Explicit); Assessment Manual V12 and the V4 schedule are legacy; no true 1RM testing; mRSI read on Wednesdays with individualized thresholds; DSI (not SJ-CMJ) steers plyo vs max strength; heavy work ends 72 h before kickoff (synthesis said 48 h); Eric sides with Issurin on residuals (speed fades first).\n- Next: apply those changes to the baseline and synthesis rev 3; stage the UE and LE rehab templates (`Downloads\\Baylor UE/LE Rehab Program Template.docx`) for the RTP synthesis; DSI needs an evidence check; constraints-led coaching primer is a request from Eric (Q25).\n- Jev Drive-triage pilot (TypeSafe_Sandbox PR branch `worktree-drive-triage-run`): FAIL on the 90% bar (76.5%), but Jev beat Haiku on every measure. **Eric's decision 2026-09-28: Jev does the Flint pass**, keeping Eric's shortlist approval step. Codex comparator 98/200, paused for memory.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3122,"cache_read_input_tokens":187758,"output_tokens":921,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3122,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":921,"cache_read_input_tokens":187758,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3122,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3122},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01YP86fALTmxcG4Rk6brpfQL":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\Flint\\.claude\\worktrees\\step1-triage\\docs\\STATUS.md","old_string":"Read this first. Update it before ending every session.\n","new_string":"Read this first. Update it before ending every session.\n\n## Method interview (2026-09-28): DONE, answers not yet applied\n- Eric answered all 27 interview-prep questions and the 6 peaking questions (merged to 30): `docs/interview/2026-09-28-method-interview.md`, in his words.\n- Its last section lists every change for `method-baseline.md` and the peaking synthesis. Biggest: course positions are Eric's (Explicit); Assessment Manual V12 and the V4 schedule are legacy; no true 1RM testing; mRSI read on Wednesdays with individualized thresholds; DSI (not SJ-CMJ) steers plyo vs max strength; heavy work ends 72 h before kickoff (synthesis said 48 h); Eric sides with Issurin on residuals (speed fades first).\n- Next: apply those changes to the baseline and synthesis rev 3; stage the UE and LE rehab templates (`Downloads\\Baylor UE/LE Rehab Program Template.docx`) for the RTP synthesis; DSI needs an evidence check; constraints-led coaching primer is a request from Eric (Q25).\n- Jev Drive-triage pilot (TypeSafe_Sandbox PR branch `worktree-drive-triage-run`): FAIL on the 90% bar (76.5%), but Jev beat Haiku on every measure. **Eric's decision 2026-09-28: Jev does the Flint pass**, keeping Eric's shortlist approval step. Codex comparator 98/200, paused for memory.\n"}},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfWFu5N18z9BDPxaCCbpH","type":"assistant","uuid":"96558a1b-49fe-481a-a932-91046005e579","timestamp":"2026-09-28T17:48:07.278Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"e054b45d-33cd-4562-af51-7c3370696c58","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\Flint\\.claude\\worktrees\\step1-triage","sessionId":"e054b45d-33cd-4562-af51-7c3370696c58","version":"2.1.283","gitBranch":"step1-triage"}
{"parentUuid":"96558a1b-49fe-481a-a932-91046005e579","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"0346e074-6d88-4c4e-a924-8e369320fddb","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YP86fALTmxcG4Rk6brpfQL","type":"tool_result","content":"The file C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\Flint\\.claude\\worktrees\\step1-triage\\docs\\STATUS.md has been updated successfully."}]},"uuid":"daf400d9-b3d4-46cf-b170-15b00421c5af","timestamp":"2026-09-28T17:48:08.321Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\Flint\\.claude\\worktrees\\step1-triage\\docs\\STATUS.md","oldString":"Read this first. Update it before ending every session.\n","newString":"Read this first. Update it before ending every session.\n\n## Method interview (2026-09-28): DONE, answers not yet applied\n- Eric answered all 27 interview-prep questions and the 6 peaking questions (merged to 30): `docs/interview/2026-09-28-method-interview.md`, in his words.\n- Its last section lists every change for `method-baseline.md` and the peaking synthesis. Biggest: course positions are Eric's (Explicit); Assessment Manual V12 and the V4 schedule are legacy; no true 1RM testing; mRSI read on Wednesdays with individualized thresholds; DSI (not SJ-CMJ) steers plyo vs max strength; heavy work ends 72 h before kickoff (synthesis said 48 h); Eric sides with Issurin on residuals (speed fades first).\n- Next: apply those changes to the baseline and synthesis rev 3; stage the UE and LE rehab templates (`Downloads\\Baylor UE/LE Rehab Program Template.docx`) for the RTP synthesis; DSI needs an evidence check; constraints-led coaching primer is a request from Eric (Q25).\n- Jev Drive-triage pilot (TypeSafe_Sandbox PR branch `worktree-drive-triage-run`): FAIL on the 90% bar (76.5%), but Jev beat Haiku on every measure. **Eric's decision 2026-09-28: Jev does the Flint pass**, keeping Eric's shortlist approval step. Codex comparator 98/200, paused for memory.\n","originalFile":"# STATUS\n\n> **Latest handoff: `docs/handoffs/2026-09-28-flint-day3.md`**. All four staged batches now pass the gate: Issurin Ch4, Zatsiorsky Ch1-2, and *Supertraining* 4.1 plus 4.2. **Promoted to the vault 2026-09-28 (SecondBrain `ab3f042`, Eric's direct approval to the orchestrator):** 68 entries (Supertraining 4.1-4.2: 41; Issurin Ch4: 10; Zatsiorsky 2e Ch1-2: 17, new book) plus 42 reciprocal links and 2 manual edits; S&C `_domain.md` merged; staging synced back (0 drift); memsearch re-index started. Peaking synthesis rev 2 is waiting on Eric's six questions.\n\nRead this first. Update it before ending every session.\n\n## Phase 2 triage (2026-09-28): shortlists drafted, waiting on Eric\n- All 3,998 files the rules left over are labelled (tier A 97, B 2,363, C 1,538). They passed round-1 review, a round-2 check (GO AFTER FIXES, applied) and a dedup.\n- Draft tier-A shortlists: `docs/shortlists/` (14 disciplines, 97 files, 84 new to the queue). The README holds totals, a throughput estimate and 8 decisions for Eric.\n- Handoff with the review record and gotchas: `docs/handoffs/2026-09-28-flint-triage.md`.\n- Next: **(Eric)** approve the shortlists, then move the approved sources into `docs/QUEUE.md`.\n\n## Day 3 (2026-09-28): gate done, promotion pending Eric\n- **Passed the gate, in staging only:**\n  - Issurin Ch4 (10 entries).\n  - Zatsiorsky 2e Ch1-2 (17 entries, new book).\n  - *Supertraining* 4.1 (6), 4.2a (15) and 4.2b (20).\n- **Review process:** each batch had an independent round-2 reviewer, not the fixer. Corrections were applied verbatim and are logged in `staging/fixes_*_applied.md`.\n- **Promotion dry run:** 69 new files. The only changed files are the two `_book.md`s. Unresolved links: 0.\n- **Ready to apply after promotion:**\n  - Reciprocal links: `staging/reciprocal_links_2026-09-28.md` (42 rows, 2 manual edits).\n  - `_domain.md` merge text: `staging/_domain_merge_sc_2026-09-28.md`.\n- **Vault:** unchanged. The last vault commit is still `aacbccd`.\n- **CVASPS transcript:** proposals are in `docs/cvasps-corroboration-proposals.md`. Its ASR check is not done: 47 flagged spots need listening before anything is cited.\n\n## Current state (2026-09-27, end of day 2)\n- **In the vault (SecondBrain `aacbccd`, pushed 2026-09-27):** 269 entries across 6 sources, all through the two-stage review gate, plus 66 reciprocal links. Staging was synced back from the vault (a promote dry run shows 0 changed).\n\n  | Book | Entries | Gate |\n  |---|---|---|\n  | Harries *On-Field RTP* (`rehab-and-return-to-play/on-field-rtp--harries`) | 37 (33 + batch 2) | 2 rounds; batch 2: 1 round |\n  | Old Bull (`performance-technology-and-leadership/old-bull-performance-course--old-bull`), new domain | 37 | 2 rounds |\n  | Issurin *Block Periodization* Ch1-3 (`block-periodization--issurin`) | 28 | Ch1-2: 2 rounds; Ch3: 1 round |\n  | Bondarchuk *Transfer of Training* I, Ch1-2 (`transfer-of-training-in-sports--bondarchuk`) | 20 | 2 rounds |\n  | *Supertraining* Ch1-3 (`supertraining--verkhoshansky`) | 113 | Ch1: 3 rounds; Ch2-3a: 2; Ch3b: 1 |\n  | Landon Evans *Elite Sports Performance* (`elite-sports-performance--evans`) | 34 | 2 rounds |\n\n- **Search index:** memsearch re-indexed 2026-09-27; spot checks return the new Issurin, Evans, Old Bull and Supertraining Ch3 entries as top hits.\n- *Supertraining* is atomized through Chapter 3 (113 entries). Resume at Ch4 (printed 201, PDF idx 212).\n- CFTS OCR done 2026-09-27: `staging/ocr/cfts--francis.md` (218 pages, 0 low-confidence, 12 blank), so F3 in the queue is unblocked. Zatsiorsky 2e OCR (`bash scripts/ocr_zatsiorsky_2e_chunks.sh`, skips finished chunks) were rerun one at a time and both finished 2026-09-27 (CVASPS transcript: `staging/transcripts/landonevansphysicalpreparationinthencaaacomplementaryapproach.md`, unchecked draft).\n- Branch `step1-triage` holds all of this (pushed). `main` needs the draft PR merged.\n\n- **OCR sources checked 2026-09-27.** Zatsiorsky 2e (`staging/ocr/science-practice-strength-2e--zatsiorsky--p*.md`, all 247 pages): the scan is missing about 2 printed pages in Ch10 (printed 205-214) and most of the Glossary and Suggested Readings (printed 227-238); Ch1-9 and Ch11 are complete (printed = PDF viewer page - 9 through PDF 213). Its OCR interleaves columns and sidebars, so read from page images. *CFTS* (`staging/ocr/cfts--francis.md`): all 11 chapters present in order; 12 blank pages are chapter-divider backs; no printed page numbers, so a missing page inside a chapter can only be caught by reading continuity; upside-down lines, dropped lines and figures are garbled despite \"0 low-confidence\". The OCR script (`scripts/ocr_pdf.py`) needs better column and rotation handling before the next scanned book.\n\n## Next\n1. **Promotion is done.** For the next book (or a book already in the vault), repeat the recipe: `scripts/promote_to_vault.py` (dry run, then `--apply`), merge `_domain.md` by hand, `scripts/apply_reciprocal_links.py`, commit and push SecondBrain, `memsearch index`, then `scripts/sync_back_from_vault.py` and commit in Flint.\n2. Merge the `step1-triage` draft PR into `main`.\n3. Add Eric's annotation to the vault Issurin 2016 brief: its \"concentrated unidirectional\" model is Verkhoshansky's, not Issurin's A-T-R (pp. 6-7, 11).\n4. Missing ideas logged by reviewers (in `staging/fixes_*_applied.md` and `staging/review_*.md`): a next atomizer batch per book. Biggest: Supertraining 3.3.3 strength and speed; Issurin's five Ch1-2 ideas; Harries speed prescription (kept inside broken-stride).\n5. Continue the queue (`docs/QUEUE.md`): *Supertraining* Ch4-9, Bondarchuk Vol I Ch3, then Zatsiorsky, Francis (CFTS once OCR is done), other Verkhoshansky books.\n6. CVASPS transcript: the draft exists, and the proposals are in `docs/cvasps-corroboration-proposals.md`. Next: listen to the 47 flagged ASR spots. After that, raise the 4 proposed Evans entries from `untested` to `supported` and atomize the new ideas.\n7. Jev pilot: build the state for the 200 files and write Claude's blind answer key.\n\n## Open questions\n- Should the Mike Golden library (1,245 files) get the same priority as TB and Landon?\n- Interview (when Eric has time): `docs/interview-prep.md`, 27 questions. New: slide U4 L1 p.16 (Evans) has \"no more than 4x per year\" body-composition testing, which may be the origin of the same rule in `method-baseline.md`.\n- Evans Verkhoshansky activation-levels entry: the slides contradict themselves on where the threshold of adaptability sits; both are recorded and the entry stays `untested` (the course ceiling) rather than `contested`. Eric's call.\n- Two-a-day entry (Issurin): confirm the current NCAA Division I preseason practice rule before using it for fall camp.\n\n## Answered\n- **How to edit this worktree** (open question from 2026-09-26): enter the existing worktree by path (`EnterWorktree` with `.claude/worktrees/step1-triage`). The local sources (`staging/books`, `staging/ocr`, `staging/audio`, `staging/sources`) exist only there.\n\n## Gotchas\n- **After promotion the vault copy is canonical.** Reciprocal links and `_domain.md` merges are written in the vault only, so staging is synced back from it (Next 1.5). When re-promoting a book that is already in the vault (Supertraining after Ch4, Harries batch 3), any file the dry run reports as \"changed\" that you did not edit in staging means investigate, not copy: `--apply` would overwrite the vault version and drop its links.\n- **Fixer logs can overstate.** One Bondarchuk fixer log claimed fixes that were not in the files. Round-2 reviewers check the files, and fixers paste grep output. Run the lint (`python scripts/lint_library.py staging/library/<domain>/<book>` for body em dashes, review-history words, confidence and sections; `scripts/promote_to_vault.py` dry run for links) before promoting.\n- **Section headers** use the vault form `**What it is** —`. Agents drifted to `: mandatory` and `- mandatory` suffixes; normalized 2026-09-27.\n- **Reviewer \"(verify)\" citations** come from model memory. Never insert one unless the vault or the paper confirms it.\n- **Background jobs die with the session.** Run long OCR in `--pages` chunks to separate files (Zatsiorsky 2e is 247 pages, about 3 hours) so a death loses one chunk. CFTS: 218 pages, about 2.5 hours.\n- **Page numbers.** The ingest-book extractor's `--pages` is inclusive and has a `viewer_page` field (claude-skills PR #9). Entries cite the 0-based `page` (= `viewer_page` minus 1). The Mac needs `git pull` in `~/.claude/skills`, then the sync script.\n- **Codex runs on Eric's ChatGPT plan cap.** When capped, reviews use fresh Opus agents with `staging/review_book_prompt.md`.\n- **Every atomizer follows `docs/ATOMIZE_BRIEF.md`**, which now carries the 2026-09-27 lessons.\n- **`staging/` tracking.** `library/`, `review_*.md`, `*_prompt.md`, `fixes_*.md`, `reciprocal_links_*.md` and `_scope_*.txt` are committed. Books, audio, sources and OCR stay local.\n- **`gws` output.** It prints \"Using keyring backend\" on stdout, and scripts filter that line out.\n- **TB attribution.** TB is shortcut-linked inside AP & Sports Science. The manifest skips shortcuts to other configured roots so TB keeps its own attribution.\n- **Triage patterns.** The rules match underscores as spaces, so folder-name patterns use `.` in place of `_`.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":4,"oldLines":6,"newStart":4,"newLines":12,"lines":[" "," Read this first. Update it before ending every session."," ","+## Method interview (2026-09-28): DONE, answers not yet applied","+- Eric answered all 27 interview-prep questions and the 6 peaking questions (merged to 30): `docs/interview/2026-09-28-method-interview.md`, in his words.","+- Its last section lists every change for `method-baseline.md` and the peaking synthesis. Biggest: course positions are Eric's (Explicit); Assessment Manual V12 and the V4 schedule are legacy; no true 1RM testing; mRSI read on Wednesdays with individualized thresholds; DSI (not SJ-CMJ) steers plyo vs max strength; heavy work ends 72 h before kickoff (synthesis said 48 h); Eric sides with Issurin on residuals (speed fades first).","+- Next: apply those changes to the baseline and synthesis rev 3; stage the UE and LE rehab templates (`Downloads\\Baylor UE/LE Rehab Program Template.docx`) for the RTP synthesis; DSI needs an evidence check; constraints-led coaching primer is a request from Eric (Q25).","+- Jev Drive-triage pilot (TypeSafe_Sandbox PR branch `worktree-drive-triage-run`): FAIL on the 90% bar (76.5%), but Jev beat Haiku on every measure. **Eric's decision 2026-09-28: Jev does the Flint pass**, keeping Eric's shortlist approval step. Codex comparator 98/200, paused for memory.","+"," ## Phase 2 triage (2026-09-28): shortlists drafted, waiting on Eric"," - All 3,998 files the rules left over are labelled (tier A 97, B 2,363, C 1,538). They passed round-1 review, a round-2 check (GO AFTER FIXES, applied) and a dedup."," - Draft tier-A shortlists: `docs/shortlists/` (14 disciplines, 97 files, 84 new to the queue). The README holds totals, a throughput estimate and 8 decisions for Eric."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false,"contentNotInModelContext":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"96558a1b-49fe-481a-a932-91046005e579","session_id":"e054b45d-33cd-4562-af51-7c3370696c58","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\Flint\\.claude\\worktrees\\step1-triage","sessionId":"e054b45d-33cd-4562-af51-7c3370696c58","version":"2.1.283","gitBranch":"step1-triage"}
