{"parentUuid":"a4be6f71-01c0-4c75-b05e-e70e783d46fc","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfWFvLqSTAmCDuMcTgTr2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1277,"cache_read_input_tokens":190880,"output_tokens":918,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":150},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1277,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":918,"cache_read_input_tokens":190880,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1277,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1277},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfWFvLPepEisCmgvidmHW","type":"assistant","uuid":"ce701d84-8b26-4ee4-87bb-cf9874e09d23","timestamp":"2026-09-28T17:48:27.739Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"e054b45d-33cd-4562-af51-7c3370696c58","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\Flint\\.claude\\worktrees\\step1-triage","sessionId":"e054b45d-33cd-4562-af51-7c3370696c58","version":"2.1.283","gitBranch":"step1-triage"}
{"parentUuid":"ce701d84-8b26-4ee4-87bb-cf9874e09d23","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfWFvLqSTAmCDuMcTgTr2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The interview is done: all 30 questions answered and recorded in your words in `Flint/docs/interview/2026-09-28-method-interview.md`. The Flint `STATUS.md` records it too. Everything is committed and pushed on `step1-triage` (`88c103b`).\n\n**What changed in Flint:**\n- **Your own method is now on record.** The course positions (Vermeil, undulating periodization, Dynamic Correspondence, the football energy-system stack) are marked as yours. You also stated your rule for any test or tool: if it doesn't answer a question someone has, it has no place.\n- **Much of the old baseline turns out to be legacy.** That covers the Assessment Manual, the V4 schedule, 1RM testing and TMG. So the baseline was describing documents more than current practice.\n- **The peaking synthesis gets a real game week.** Hard work ends 72 hours before kickoff, speed is treated as fading first (Issurin), and bye weeks are sorted by snap count.\n\n**Where your answers show gaps.** Several answers were \"nothing formal\": GPS thresholds, a risk model, recovery tracking, a readiness assessment, data going to nutrition, reports built by Applied Performance. Many departments share those gaps, so they aren't failings on their own. But together they're a clear map of where Applied Performance could add value, which fits your OKR-driven push. I'd treat that list as a candidate agenda rather than just baseline notes.\n\n**Not done yet:**\n- The answers are **recorded but not yet applied** to `method-baseline.md` or the peaking synthesis. The last section of the interview file lists every edit.\n- The Jev pilot write-up in TypeSafe (STATUS, capability map, draft PR) is still pending.\n- Codex is paused at 98 of 200.\n\n**Next, in the order I'd do them:**\n1. Apply your answers to the baseline and write peaking synthesis rev 3, with one subagent.\n2. Stage your UE and LE rehab templates for the RTP synthesis.\n3. Write up the Jev pilot and open the draft PR.\n4. Restart Codex once memsearch is idle.\n5. A primer on constraints-led coaching, which you asked for in question 25. It would come from your library first.\n\nSay which, or \"all\", and I'll run them one at a time to keep memory down."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1277,"cache_read_input_tokens":190880,"output_tokens":918,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":150},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1277,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":918,"cache_read_input_tokens":190880,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1277,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1277},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfWFvLPepEisCmgvidmHW","type":"assistant","uuid":"f2dd76b7-79e9-42c8-ae66-6dd9961a4517","timestamp":"2026-09-28T17:48:28.433Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"e054b45d-33cd-4562-af51-7c3370696c58","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\Flint\\.claude\\worktrees\\step1-triage","sessionId":"e054b45d-33cd-4562-af51-7c3370696c58","version":"2.1.283","gitBranch":"step1-triage"}
