{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-09-28T18:10:15.658Z","sessionId":"e054b45d-33cd-4562-af51-7c3370696c58","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a2efa862e6ed8c50e</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_019zU1dFDrcR39ihx59KNuds</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Users-eric-rash-Desktop-DEV-Flint--claude-worktrees-step1-triage\\e054b45d-33cd-4562-af51-7c3370696c58\\tasks\\a2efa862e6ed8c50e.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Apply interview answers to Flint docs\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>I've applied all of Eric's interview answers and committed them on step1-triage in two commits, 5545f06 and 4ac2693. Nothing was pushed, and the vault was not touched.\n\n**`docs/method-baseline.md`**\n- **Inferred to Explicit:** 3 bullets (Vermeil hierarchy, undulating periodization, Dynamic Correspondence). The football energy-system stack was already Explicit; I added that he claimed it again in Q1.\n- **Legacy:** 11 bullets. That covers 7 from Assessment Manual V12, the V4 table (Q9 says it was never used), the 1RM assumptions, TMG (Chris Ruf with Track only) and the five expectations.\n- **Superseded:** 2 bullets from his own slides. The body-size heart-rate table (pp.28-29) is replaced by his age-based answer (Q20). The \"aerobic lost first\" slide (p.47) is replaced by his Issurin answer (Q16).\n- **New:** 26 bullets covering every item on your list, plus Q5 (\"Both\") and Q25 (constraints-led coaching not used).\n- **Tensions:** each of the original 10 now has a status line. Resolved: 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 9, and 1 partly. Still open: 7, 8, 10. I added new tensions 11 to 16.\n- **Thin flags:** injury risk, recovery and nutrition now say plainly that nothing formal exists. RTP has a stated role, but its written protocol (the UE and LE templates) is not staged yet.\n- The provenance key has the new tags, and the named-influences table now credits Eric for Vermeil, Verkhoshansky and Parker, and has a new Issurin row.\n\n**Peaking synthesis rev 3 (dated 2026-09-28)**\n- Section 8 is replaced with his answers.\n- The bottom line now uses his real week, with 72 h replacing the 48 h rev 2 guessed.\n- The Monday heavy lift at about 48 h post-game is recorded as a labelled tension against Norris 2019 and Cosio 2026, with no verdict.\n- Bottom line 4 now gives his Issurin position and keeps the counter-evidence. Sections 4, 6 and 7 are updated, and no new evidence was added.\n\n**`docs/interview-prep.md`:** one-line completion note at the top pointing to the answers file.\n\n**Answers I could not map cleanly**\n- **Q7:** he said thresholds do not exist \"formally\". The question also asked about informal ones, and that half went unanswered.\n- **Peaking Q3, second half:** the course's in-season rule (\"maintain intensity, reduce volume\") was never claimed.\n- **Peaking Q6:** whether the postseason gets its own taper was not answered.\n- **Q18:** he doesn't have the in-season sets and reps.\n- **Q21:** he answered with DSI (CMJ against mid-thigh pull), not the SJ-CMJ gap the question asked about. DSI has no evidence check in the library yet.\n\n**Contradictions**\n- **His answers against his own teaching:** Q16 and Q20 each contradict slides from a session he taught himself (p.47 and pp.28-29).\n- **Q2 against SportSmith:** he names a Wednesday mRSI read, but his SportSmith piece describes daily mRSI readiness.\n- **Q22 against Q2:** \"We don't assess readiness\" (in RTP) sits against mRSI as his readiness marker.\n- **Q4 against the Playbook:** \"It doesn't really end\" goes further than the Playbook's \"support\" framing.\n- **Q3 against Q12:** by his own rule, a test that answers no question has no place. Yet the staff still look at ACWR (\"we dabble\") while he doesn't trust it, and movement screens are collected without changing decisions.\n- **Q10 against %1RM loading:** no sport tests a true 1RM, yet the loading charts in his course material are written as percentages of it. So in practice those loads rest on projected maxes.\n\nThe synthesis's revision log in `_work/review_peaking_synthesis_opus.md` still stops at rev 2, and `docs/STATUS.md` is not updated.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>148925</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>83</tool_uses><duration_ms>571754</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
