{"parentUuid":"b5217648-59e7-4803-8272-4d33761239b0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfWHeBCYTDM8aJvTj8c7S","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FVSvG67DFyRRf8LXM1xE7n","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\Flint\\.claude\\worktrees\\step1-triage\\staging\\rtp\\Baylor UE Rehab Program Template.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":425,"cache_read_input_tokens":201871,"output_tokens":217,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":425,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":217,"cache_read_input_tokens":201871,"cache_creation_input_tokens":425,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":425},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01FVSvG67DFyRRf8LXM1xE7n":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\Flint\\.claude\\worktrees\\step1-triage\\staging\\rtp\\Baylor UE Rehab Program Template.md"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfWHeAhnaawPxemGwQfL4","type":"assistant","uuid":"340a5122-22f2-47b5-a24b-3e36518da5c0","timestamp":"2026-09-28T18:10:54.617Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"e054b45d-33cd-4562-af51-7c3370696c58","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\Flint\\.claude\\worktrees\\step1-triage","sessionId":"e054b45d-33cd-4562-af51-7c3370696c58","version":"2.1.283","gitBranch":"step1-triage"}
{"parentUuid":"b5217648-59e7-4803-8272-4d33761239b0","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"2876ffd3-8d74-4539-a14c-a9a62bf4476e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Mvk48EezBwEZTuor24ujEj","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tOverview\n2\tChecklist\n3\t| Phase | Milestones | Date |\n4\t| Healing | Pain <3/10 / ROM Progress  / Muscle activation / Effusion/swelling grading |  |\n5\t| Healing | Surgical report/imaging  / Mental Health Check-In  / Nutrition Check-In |  |\n6\t| Foundation | ROM: Symmetrical to uninvolved limb / Gait: Normalized, pain-free / SLSB (EO/EC) and Y- Balance Anterior Reach ≥90% / Symmetry Squat Competency ≥90% / FMS > 14 |  |\n7\t| Reconstruction | HHD ≥80% LSI / IMTP ≥80% / Hop test battery ≥80% / SL Squat & SL Calf Raise ≥80% |  |\n8\t| Reintegration | HHD ≥90% LSI / IMTP ≥90% / Hop test battery ≥90% / CMJ / Drop Jump |  |\n9\t| Evaluation | SLJ / 10-yard sprint  / COD: 10-5 Test / Workload 100% |  |\n10\t| Evaluation | Subjective Questionnaire  / Physician clearance  / Mental Health Check-In  / Nutrition Check-In |  |\n11\t| Competition | Competition tolerance: pain/swelling |  |\n12\t\n13\tProgramming\n14\t## Healing – Prepare for Activity (Time)\n15\t| Healing – Prepare for Activity: Recovery (Time) / Primary: AT, PT | Secondary: Nutrition, Mental Health, S&C |\n16\t| Training Block | Goals | Weekly Plan |\n17\t| Block 1.1 (Time) | Pain/swelling control, ROM per protocol, quad activation | High-frequency mobility, muscle activation, accessory movements |\n18\t| Block 1.2 (Time) | Achieve full extension, ROM per protocol, progress isometrics | 3 endurance sessions+ 2 pool/mobility |\n19\t| Notes |\n20\t|  |\n21\t\n22\t## Foundation – Prepare to Train (Time)\n23\t| Foundation – Prepare to Train: ROM and movement quality (Time) / Primary: AT, PT, S&C | Secondary: Nutrition, Mental Health |\n24\t| Training Block | Goals | Weekly Plan |\n25\t| Block 2.1 (Time) | Full ROM, progress WB, light closed chain strength, proprioceptive drills | 3 endurance + 2 balance/mobility |\n26\t| Block 2.2 (Time) | Normalize gait, progress closed-chain strength, controlled single-leg loading, balance progressions | 3 strength + 2 balance/conditioning |\n27\t| Notes |\n28\t|  |\n29\t\n30\t## Reconstruction – Prepare for Practice (Time)\n31\t| Reconstruction – Prepare for Practice: Strength, symmetry, and fitness (Time) / Primary: AT, PT, S&C | Secondary: Nutrition, Mental Health, Sport Coach |\n32\t| Training Block | Goals | Weekly Plan |\n33\t| Block 3.1 (Time) | Normalize strength base, quadriceps/hamstrings strength ≥65–70% symmetry, dynamic balance | 3 strength + 2 balance |\n34\t| Block 3.2 (Time) | Advance bilateral → unilateral strength, introduce low-level plyos | 3 strength/power + 2 plyometrics/running |\n35\t| Block 3.3 (Time) | Develop power, progress plyometrics, linear agility, quadriceps/hamstrings strength ≥75–80% symmetry | 3 strength/power + 2 agility/plyometrics |\n36\t| Notes |\n37\t|  |\n38\t\n39\t## Reintegration – Prepare for Game Speed (Time)\n40\t| Reintegration – Prepare for Game Speed: RFD, COD, technical skills (Time) / Primary: S&C, Sport Coach | Secondary: AT, PT, Nutrition, Mental Health |\n41\t| Training Block | Goals | Weekly Plan |\n42\t| Block 4.1 (Time) | Advance agility (linear + lateral), introduce cutting drills | 2 strength/power + reactive agility |\n43\t| Block 4.2 (Time) | Integrate into non-contact practice, strength and Hop test symmetry ≥90% | 2 strength/power + 2 reactive agility + practice integration |\n44\t| Notes |\n45\t|  |\n46\t\n47\t## Evaluation – Prepare for Competition (Time)\n48\t| Evaluation – Prepare for Competition: Maximal and sustained outputs (Time) / Primary: S&C, Sport Coach | Secondary: AT, Nutrition, Mental Health |\n49\t| Training Block | Goals | Weekly Plan |\n50\t| Block 5 (Time) | Full contact practice, game-like demands, psychological readiness | Maintenance + load monitoring |\n51\t| Notes |\n52\t|  |\n53\t\n54\t## Competition (Time)\n55\t| Competition: Maintenance and load management (Time) / Primary: Sport Coach | Secondary: S&C, Nutrition, Mental Health |\n56\t| Training Block | Goals | Weekly Plan |\n57\t| Block 6 (Time) | Competition integration, prevention, load monitoring | Maintenance |\n58\t| Notes |\n59\t|  |\n60\t\n61\t## Appendix 1 (Testing)\n62\tTesting Metrics\n63\tSingle Leg Stand (SLSB)\n64\tTotal Excursion (mm)\n65\tTotal Excursion Asymmetry (%)\n66\tY-Balance\n67\tNormalized Reach Score (%)\n68\tComposite Score (%)\n69\tSquat Assessment\n70\tEccentric Peak Force Asymmetry (%)\n71\tConcentric Peak Force Asymmetry (%)\n72\tSquat depth (cm)\n73\tIsometric Mid-Thigh Pull (IMTP) or Isometric Belt Squat\n74\tPeak Vertical Force/BM (N/kg)\n75\tPeak Vertical Force Asymmetry (%)\n76\tHop test battery\n77\tHopscotch (4 square hops)\n78\tAsymmetry CW/CCW (%)\n79\tSL Broad Jump\n80\tJump distance (in.)\n81\tDistance asymmetry (%)\n82\tSL Triple Jump\n83\tJump distance (in.)\n84\tDistance asymmetry (%)\n85\tSpeed Hop (6m or 20ft)\n86\tTime (sec.)\n87\tTime asymmetry (%)\n88\tCountermovement Jump (CMJ)\n89\tPerformance Metrics\n90\tJump height (cm)\n91\tEccentric Braking Impulse (Ns)\n92\tContraction Time (ms)\n93\tConcentric Mean Power/BW (W/kg)\n94\tEccentric Peak Velocity\n95\tSet a minimum threshold of -1.25 m/s as quality control for the test\n96\tAsymmetry Metrics\n97\tEccentric Braking Impulse Asymmetry (%)\n98\tConcentric Impulse Asymmetry (%)\n99\tDrop Jump\n100\tDrop height based on their current (meaning during rehab) CMJ height\n101\tForce plates are 2.25\" high - factor into drop height\n102\tPerformance Metrics\n103\tContact Time (sec.)\n104\tJump Height:Drop Height\n105\tRSI\n106\tAsymmetry Metrics\n107\tPeak Landing Force Asymmetry (%)\n108\tActive Stiffness Asymmetry (%)\n109\tEccentric Impulse Asymmetry (%)\n110\tConcentric Impulse Asymmetry (%)\n111\tSingle Leg Jump (SLJ)\n112\tPerformance Metrics\n113\tJump height (cm)\n114\tEccentric Braking Impulse (Ns)\n115\tContraction Time (ms)\n116\tConcentric Mean Power/BW (W/kg)\n117\tEccentric Peak Velocity\n118\tSet a minimum threshold of -1.25 m/s as quality control for the test\n119\tAsymmetry Metrics\n120\tEccentric Braking Impulse Asymmetry (%)\n121\tConcentric Impulse Asymmetry (%)\n122\tSprint Testing\n123\t10 yard accel\n124\tHave to test in accordance with how that sport tests - meaning same setup, start position and trigger\n125\t10 yard fly w/20 yard run-in - sport dependent\n126\tChange of Direction\n127\t10-5 COD Asymmetry (%)\n128\t90% threshold from 10 yard accel\n129\tPro Agility (5-10-5)\n130\tCurvilinear Sprint Test - Right and Left\n131\tField sports\n132\tNeed our own standardized protocol if one doesn't exist in the literature"}]},"uuid":"e97be983-d79f-4794-90b2-a7cfa63c4f81","timestamp":"2026-09-28T18:10:54.770Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\Flint\\.claude\\worktrees\\step1-triage\\staging\\rtp\\Baylor LE Rehab Program Template.md","content":"Overview\nChecklist\n| Phase | Milestones | Date |\n| Healing | Pain <3/10 / ROM Progress  / Muscle activation / Effusion/swelling grading |  |\n| Healing | Surgical report/imaging  / Mental Health Check-In  / Nutrition Check-In |  |\n| Foundation | ROM: Symmetrical to uninvolved limb / Gait: Normalized, pain-free / SLSB (EO/EC) and Y- Balance Anterior Reach ≥90% / Symmetry Squat Competency ≥90% / FMS > 14 |  |\n| Reconstruction | HHD ≥80% LSI / IMTP ≥80% / Hop test battery ≥80% / SL Squat & SL Calf Raise ≥80% |  |\n| Reintegration | HHD ≥90% LSI / IMTP ≥90% / Hop test battery ≥90% / CMJ / Drop Jump |  |\n| Evaluation | SLJ / 10-yard sprint  / COD: 10-5 Test / Workload 100% |  |\n| Evaluation | Subjective Questionnaire  / Physician clearance  / Mental Health Check-In  / Nutrition Check-In |  |\n| Competition | Competition tolerance: pain/swelling |  |\n\nProgramming\n## Healing – Prepare for Activity (Time)\n| Healing – Prepare for Activity: Recovery (Time) / Primary: AT, PT | Secondary: Nutrition, Mental Health, S&C |\n| Training Block | Goals | Weekly Plan |\n| Block 1.1 (Time) | Pain/swelling control, ROM per protocol, quad activation | High-frequency mobility, muscle activation, accessory movements |\n| Block 1.2 (Time) | Achieve full extension, ROM per protocol, progress isometrics | 3 endurance sessions+ 2 pool/mobility |\n| Notes |\n|  |\n\n## Foundation – Prepare to Train (Time)\n| Foundation – Prepare to Train: ROM and movement quality (Time) / Primary: AT, PT, S&C | Secondary: Nutrition, Mental Health |\n| Training Block | Goals | Weekly Plan |\n| Block 2.1 (Time) | Full ROM, progress WB, light closed chain strength, proprioceptive drills | 3 endurance + 2 balance/mobility |\n| Block 2.2 (Time) | Normalize gait, progress closed-chain strength, controlled single-leg loading, balance progressions | 3 strength + 2 balance/conditioning |\n| Notes |\n|  |\n\n## Reconstruction – Prepare for Practice (Time)\n| Reconstruction – Prepare for Practice: Strength, symmetry, and fitness (Time) / Primary: AT, PT, S&C | Secondary: Nutrition, Mental Health, Sport Coach |\n| Training Block | Goals | Weekly Plan |\n| Block 3.1 (Time) | Normalize strength base, quadriceps/hamstrings strength ≥65–70% symmetry, dynamic balance | 3 strength + 2 balance |\n| Block 3.2 (Time) | Advance bilateral → unilateral strength, introduce low-level plyos | 3 strength/power + 2 plyometrics/running |\n| Block 3.3 (Time) | Develop power, progress plyometrics, linear agility, quadriceps/hamstrings strength ≥75–80% symmetry | 3 strength/power + 2 agility/plyometrics |\n| Notes |\n|  |\n\n## Reintegration – Prepare for Game Speed (Time)\n| Reintegration – Prepare for Game Speed: RFD, COD, technical skills (Time) / Primary: S&C, Sport Coach | Secondary: AT, PT, Nutrition, Mental Health |\n| Training Block | Goals | Weekly Plan |\n| Block 4.1 (Time) | Advance agility (linear + lateral), introduce cutting drills | 2 strength/power + reactive agility |\n| Block 4.2 (Time) | Integrate into non-contact practice, strength and Hop test symmetry ≥90% | 2 strength/power + 2 reactive agility + practice integration |\n| Notes |\n|  |\n\n## Evaluation – Prepare for Competition (Time)\n| Evaluation – Prepare for Competition: Maximal and sustained outputs (Time) / Primary: S&C, Sport Coach | Secondary: AT, Nutrition, Mental Health |\n| Training Block | Goals | Weekly Plan |\n| Block 5 (Time) | Full contact practice, game-like demands, psychological readiness | Maintenance + load monitoring |\n| Notes |\n|  |\n\n## Competition (Time)\n| Competition: Maintenance and load management (Time) / Primary: Sport Coach | Secondary: S&C, Nutrition, Mental Health |\n| Training Block | Goals | Weekly Plan |\n| Block 6 (Time) | Competition integration, prevention, load monitoring | Maintenance |\n| Notes |\n|  |\n\n## Appendix 1 (Testing)\nTesting Metrics\nSingle Leg Stand (SLSB)\nTotal Excursion (mm)\nTotal Excursion Asymmetry (%)\nY-Balance\nNormalized Reach Score (%)\nComposite Score (%)\nSquat Assessment\nEccentric Peak Force Asymmetry (%)\nConcentric Peak Force Asymmetry (%)\nSquat depth (cm)\nIsometric Mid-Thigh Pull (IMTP) or Isometric Belt Squat\nPeak Vertical Force/BM (N/kg)\nPeak Vertical Force Asymmetry (%)\nHop test battery\nHopscotch (4 square hops)\nAsymmetry CW/CCW (%)\nSL Broad Jump\nJump distance (in.)\nDistance asymmetry (%)\nSL Triple Jump\nJump distance (in.)\nDistance asymmetry (%)\nSpeed Hop (6m or 20ft)\nTime (sec.)\nTime asymmetry (%)\nCountermovement Jump (CMJ)\nPerformance Metrics\nJump height (cm)\nEccentric Braking Impulse (Ns)\nContraction Time (ms)\nConcentric Mean Power/BW (W/kg)\nEccentric Peak Velocity\nSet a minimum threshold of -1.25 m/s as quality control for the test\nAsymmetry Metrics\nEccentric Braking Impulse Asymmetry (%)\nConcentric Impulse Asymmetry (%)\nDrop Jump\nDrop height based on their current (meaning during rehab) CMJ height\nForce plates are 2.25\" high - factor into drop height\nPerformance Metrics\nContact Time (sec.)\nJump Height:Drop Height\nRSI\nAsymmetry Metrics\nPeak Landing Force Asymmetry (%)\nActive Stiffness Asymmetry (%)\nEccentric Impulse Asymmetry (%)\nConcentric Impulse Asymmetry (%)\nSingle Leg Jump (SLJ)\nPerformance Metrics\nJump height (cm)\nEccentric Braking Impulse (Ns)\nContraction Time (ms)\nConcentric Mean Power/BW (W/kg)\nEccentric Peak Velocity\nSet a minimum threshold of -1.25 m/s as quality control for the test\nAsymmetry Metrics\nEccentric Braking Impulse Asymmetry (%)\nConcentric Impulse Asymmetry (%)\nSprint Testing\n10 yard accel\nHave to test in accordance with how that sport tests - meaning same setup, start position and trigger\n10 yard fly w/20 yard run-in - sport dependent\nChange of Direction\n10-5 COD Asymmetry (%)\n90% threshold from 10 yard accel\nPro Agility (5-10-5)\nCurvilinear Sprint Test - Right and Left\nField sports\nNeed our own standardized protocol if one doesn't exist in the literature","numLines":132,"startLine":1,"totalLines":132}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b5217648-59e7-4803-8272-4d33761239b0","session_id":"e054b45d-33cd-4562-af51-7c3370696c58","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\Flint\\.claude\\worktrees\\step1-triage","sessionId":"e054b45d-33cd-4562-af51-7c3370696c58","version":"2.1.283","gitBranch":"step1-triage"}
{"parentUuid":"340a5122-22f2-47b5-a24b-3e36518da5c0","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"2876ffd3-8d74-4539-a14c-a9a62bf4476e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FVSvG67DFyRRf8LXM1xE7n","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tOverview\n2\tChecklist\n3\t| Phase | Milestones | Date |\n4\t| Healing | Pain <3/10 / ROM per protocol / Pain free submaximal isometrics |  |\n5\t| Healing | Surgical report/imaging  / Mental Health Check-In  / Nutrition Check-In |  |\n6\t| Foundation | Shoulder ROM WNL / ADLs pain-free / FMS >14 |  |\n7\t| Reconstruction | HHD ≥90% LSI / ASH Test ≥90% / Upper Quarter Y-Balance ≥85% symmetry |  |\n8\t| Reintegration | Plyometric push-up / Throwing: Full distance, 75-85% velocity (sport-dependent)  / Workload = 80% |  |\n9\t| Evaluation | Throwing: 100% velocity/distance pain-free (sport-dependent) / Workload = 100% |  |\n10\t| Evaluation | Subjective Questionnaire  / Physician clearance  / Mental Health Check-In  / Nutrition Check-In |  |\n11\t| Competition | Competition tolerance: pain/swelling |  |\n12\t\n13\tPrograming\n14\t## Healing – Prepare for Activity (Time)\n15\t| Healing – Prepare for Activity: Recovery (Time) / Primary: AT, PT | Secondary: Nutrition, Mental Health, S&C |\n16\t| Training Block | Goals | Weekly Plan |\n17\t| Block 1.1 (Time) | Pain/swelling control, sling weaning, PROM only, scapular training | high-frequency passive mobility (pendulums, PROM in scapular plane), isometric scapular holds, grip strengthening |\n18\t| Block 1.2 (Time) | Progress to AAROM, external rotation to neutral, initiate rhythmic stabilization | 3 endurance sessions+ 2 pool/mobility |\n19\t| Notes |\n20\t| Start aerobic conditioning and lower body |\n21\t\n22\tFoundation – Prepare to Train (Time)\n23\t| Foundation – Prepare to Train: ROM and movement quality (Time) / Primary: AT, PT, S&C | Secondary: Nutrition, Mental Health |\n24\t| Training Block | Goals | Weekly Plan |\n25\t| Block 2.1 (Time) | Full PROM, progress rotator cuff strengthening (submaximal) | 3 endurance + 2 mobility |\n26\t| Block 2.2 (Time) | AROM approaching symmetrical, strengthen rotator cuff isotonically, advance scapular stability | 3 endurance + 2 mobility |\n27\t| Notes |\n28\t| Continue aerobic conditioning – progress |\n29\t\n30\t## Reconstruction – Prepare for Practice (Time)\n31\t| Reconstruction – Prepare for Practice: Strength, symmetry, and fitness (Time) / Primary: AT, PT, S&C | Secondary: Nutrition, Mental Health, Sport Coach |\n32\t| Training Block | Goals | Weekly Plan |\n33\t| Block 3.1 (Time) | Rotator cuff/grip strength ≥80% symmetry, start CKC exercises, return to weight room | 2-3 strength sessions + 2 stability/motor control |\n34\t| Block 3.2 (Time) | Rotator cuff/grip strength ≥90% symmetry, introduce overhead loading, advance to 90/90 position work, initiate bilateral plyometrics | 2 strength/power sessions + 2 plyometric sessions |\n35\t| Block 3.3 (Time) | Develop power, initiate throwing & hitting progression (if applicable), progress to unilateral plyometrics | 2 strength/power sessions + 2 plyometric sessions |\n36\t| Notes |\n37\t\n38\t## Reintegration – Prepare for Game Speed (Time)\n39\t| Reintegration – Prepare for Game Speed: RFD, COD, technical skills (Time) / Primary: S&C, Sport Coach | Secondary: AT, PT, Nutrition, Mental Health |\n40\t| Training Block | Goals | Weekly Plan |\n41\t| Block 4.1 (Time) | Advance throwing velocity/distance, reactive plyometrics, sport-specific patterns | 3 strength/power sessions + 2 throwing/sport-specific (Phase 2 throwing, sport simulation) |\n42\t| Block 4.2 (Time) | Integrate into non-contact practice, continue throwing progression | 2 strength/power sessions + 2 throwing/sport-specific (Phase 2 throwing, sport simulation) + Practice integration |\n43\t| Notes |\n44\t\n45\t## Evaluation – Prepare for Competition (Time)\n46\t| Evaluation – Prepare for Competition: Maximal and sustained outputs (Time) / Primary: S&C, Sport Coach | Secondary: AT, Nutrition, Mental Health |\n47\t| Training Block | Goals | Weekly Plan |\n48\t| Block 5 (Time) | Full throwing velocity/full contact practice, tolerate high-volume training, game-like demands, psychological readiness | Maintenance + load monitoring |\n49\t| Notes |\n50\t\n51\tCompetition (Time)\n52\t| Competition: Maintenance and load management (Time) / Primary: Sport Coach | Secondary: S&C, Nutrition, Mental Health |\n53\t| Training Block | Goals | Weekly Plan |\n54\t| Block 6 (Time) | Competition integration, long-term prevention, pitch/throw count monitoring | Maintenance |\n55\t| Notes |\n56\t|  |\n57\t\n58\t## Appendix 1 (Testing)\n59\tASH Test Cluster: Shoulder ISO-I,T,Y\n60\tPeak Vertical Force/BM (N/kg)\n61\tPeak Vertical Force/BM asymmetry (%)\n62\tY-balance\n63\tNormalized Reach Score (%)\n64\tComposite Score (%)\n65\tPlyometric Push-up\n66\tPeak Landing Force Asymmetry (%)\n67\tEccentric Impulse Asymmetry (%)\n68\tConcentric Impulse Asymmetry (%)"}]},"uuid":"215c2fab-7edc-4999-ae0d-4192cf770476","timestamp":"2026-09-28T18:10:55.022Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\Flint\\.claude\\worktrees\\step1-triage\\staging\\rtp\\Baylor UE Rehab Program Template.md","content":"Overview\nChecklist\n| Phase | Milestones | Date |\n| Healing | Pain <3/10 / ROM per protocol / Pain free submaximal isometrics |  |\n| Healing | Surgical report/imaging  / Mental Health Check-In  / Nutrition Check-In |  |\n| Foundation | Shoulder ROM WNL / ADLs pain-free / FMS >14 |  |\n| Reconstruction | HHD ≥90% LSI / ASH Test ≥90% / Upper Quarter Y-Balance ≥85% symmetry |  |\n| Reintegration | Plyometric push-up / Throwing: Full distance, 75-85% velocity (sport-dependent)  / Workload = 80% |  |\n| Evaluation | Throwing: 100% velocity/distance pain-free (sport-dependent) / Workload = 100% |  |\n| Evaluation | Subjective Questionnaire  / Physician clearance  / Mental Health Check-In  / Nutrition Check-In |  |\n| Competition | Competition tolerance: pain/swelling |  |\n\nPrograming\n## Healing – Prepare for Activity (Time)\n| Healing – Prepare for Activity: Recovery (Time) / Primary: AT, PT | Secondary: Nutrition, Mental Health, S&C |\n| Training Block | Goals | Weekly Plan |\n| Block 1.1 (Time) | Pain/swelling control, sling weaning, PROM only, scapular training | high-frequency passive mobility (pendulums, PROM in scapular plane), isometric scapular holds, grip strengthening |\n| Block 1.2 (Time) | Progress to AAROM, external rotation to neutral, initiate rhythmic stabilization | 3 endurance sessions+ 2 pool/mobility |\n| Notes |\n| Start aerobic conditioning and lower body |\n\nFoundation – Prepare to Train (Time)\n| Foundation – Prepare to Train: ROM and movement quality (Time) / Primary: AT, PT, S&C | Secondary: Nutrition, Mental Health |\n| Training Block | Goals | Weekly Plan |\n| Block 2.1 (Time) | Full PROM, progress rotator cuff strengthening (submaximal) | 3 endurance + 2 mobility |\n| Block 2.2 (Time) | AROM approaching symmetrical, strengthen rotator cuff isotonically, advance scapular stability | 3 endurance + 2 mobility |\n| Notes |\n| Continue aerobic conditioning – progress |\n\n## Reconstruction – Prepare for Practice (Time)\n| Reconstruction – Prepare for Practice: Strength, symmetry, and fitness (Time) / Primary: AT, PT, S&C | Secondary: Nutrition, Mental Health, Sport Coach |\n| Training Block | Goals | Weekly Plan |\n| Block 3.1 (Time) | Rotator cuff/grip strength ≥80% symmetry, start CKC exercises, return to weight room | 2-3 strength sessions + 2 stability/motor control |\n| Block 3.2 (Time) | Rotator cuff/grip strength ≥90% symmetry, introduce overhead loading, advance to 90/90 position work, initiate bilateral plyometrics | 2 strength/power sessions + 2 plyometric sessions |\n| Block 3.3 (Time) | Develop power, initiate throwing & hitting progression (if applicable), progress to unilateral plyometrics | 2 strength/power sessions + 2 plyometric sessions |\n| Notes |\n\n## Reintegration – Prepare for Game Speed (Time)\n| Reintegration – Prepare for Game Speed: RFD, COD, technical skills (Time) / Primary: S&C, Sport Coach | Secondary: AT, PT, Nutrition, Mental Health |\n| Training Block | Goals | Weekly Plan |\n| Block 4.1 (Time) | Advance throwing velocity/distance, reactive plyometrics, sport-specific patterns | 3 strength/power sessions + 2 throwing/sport-specific (Phase 2 throwing, sport simulation) |\n| Block 4.2 (Time) | Integrate into non-contact practice, continue throwing progression | 2 strength/power sessions + 2 throwing/sport-specific (Phase 2 throwing, sport simulation) + Practice integration |\n| Notes |\n\n## Evaluation – Prepare for Competition (Time)\n| Evaluation – Prepare for Competition: Maximal and sustained outputs (Time) / Primary: S&C, Sport Coach | Secondary: AT, Nutrition, Mental Health |\n| Training Block | Goals | Weekly Plan |\n| Block 5 (Time) | Full throwing velocity/full contact practice, tolerate high-volume training, game-like demands, psychological readiness | Maintenance + load monitoring |\n| Notes |\n\nCompetition (Time)\n| Competition: Maintenance and load management (Time) / Primary: Sport Coach | Secondary: S&C, Nutrition, Mental Health |\n| Training Block | Goals | Weekly Plan |\n| Block 6 (Time) | Competition integration, long-term prevention, pitch/throw count monitoring | Maintenance |\n| Notes |\n|  |\n\n## Appendix 1 (Testing)\nASH Test Cluster: Shoulder ISO-I,T,Y\nPeak Vertical Force/BM (N/kg)\nPeak Vertical Force/BM asymmetry (%)\nY-balance\nNormalized Reach Score (%)\nComposite Score (%)\nPlyometric Push-up\nPeak Landing Force Asymmetry (%)\nEccentric Impulse Asymmetry (%)\nConcentric Impulse Asymmetry (%)","numLines":68,"startLine":1,"totalLines":68}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"340a5122-22f2-47b5-a24b-3e36518da5c0","session_id":"e054b45d-33cd-4562-af51-7c3370696c58","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\Flint\\.clau