{"parentUuid":"fe080ade-0b32-4254-9cb0-eb67dfa0ae1e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfWHeNKnMij6AJG5mywia","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I've reviewed both templates—both are phase-based with numeric gates and a testing appendix. I found three spots that don't quite match your interview answers, so I'm noting them down.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5463,"cache_read_input_tokens":202296,"output_tokens":1449,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":408},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5463,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1449,"cache_read_input_tokens":202296,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5463,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5463},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfWHeMmYgbvC2GjTgvW8G","type":"assistant","uuid":"d792b46e-0a5a-47b3-8aca-789c09ceff3f","timestamp":"2026-09-28T18:11:00.324Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"e054b45d-33cd-4562-af51-7c3370696c58","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\Flint\\.claude\\worktrees\\step1-triage","sessionId":"e054b45d-33cd-4562-af51-7c3370696c58","version":"2.1.283","gitBranch":"step1-triage"}
{"parentUuid":"d792b46e-0a5a-47b3-8aca-789c09ceff3f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfWHeNKnMij6AJG5mywia","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MoMZ4XuxocM1BA2rPx3P9r","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\Flint\\.claude\\worktrees\\step1-triage\\docs\\interview\\2026-09-28-method-interview.md","old_string":"(Not yet staged. Next step: copy both to Drive and stage a text copy for the RTP synthesis.)","new_string":"(Staged 2026-09-28 as `staging/rtp/Baylor {UE,LE} Rehab Program Template.{docx,md}`; text\nextracted by `staging/rtp/docx_to_md.py`. The originals are only in Downloads; the LE file\nname there has a stray space before `.docx`. Both should move to Drive.)\n\nWhat the templates contain: six phases (Healing, Foundation, Reconstruction, Reintegration,\nEvaluation, Competition), each with a primary and secondary owner, training blocks and weekly\nplans, a milestone checklist, and a testing appendix. LE gates: HHD LSI, IMTP, hop battery at\n80% then 90%, CMJ, drop jump, SLJ, 10-yard sprint, 10-5 COD, workload 100%. UE gates: HHD LSI\n90%, ASH test 90%, upper-quarter Y-balance 85%, plyo push-up, throwing progression, workload\n80% then 100%. Applied Performance-relevant owners: S&C is primary from Foundation onward.\n\nThree places the templates sit against the interview (for Eric, not resolved here):\n- **COD (Q13).** \"We don't test change of direction in most sports\", but the LE template gates\n  Evaluation on the 10-5 COD test and lists pro agility and a curvilinear sprint. Reading:\n  COD is tested inside RTP, not in routine team testing.\n- **Movement screens (Q12).** \"Nothing changes decisions\", but both templates gate Foundation\n  on FMS > 14.\n- **Readiness (Q22).** \"We don't assess readiness. The template answers that.\" The template's\n  Evaluation phase is in effect a readiness gate (outputs, workload 100%, subjective\n  questionnaire, physician clearance), so the answer is better read as \"readiness is decided\n  by these criteria, not by a separate daily assessment\"."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5463,"cache_read_input_tokens":202296,"output_tokens":1449,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":408},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5463,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1449,"cache_read_input_tokens":202296,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5463,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5463},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01MoMZ4XuxocM1BA2rPx3P9r":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\Flint\\.claude\\worktrees\\step1-triage\\docs\\interview\\2026-09-28-method-interview.md","old_string":"(Not yet staged. Next step: copy both to Drive and stage a text copy for the RTP synthesis.)","new_string":"(Staged 2026-09-28 as `staging/rtp/Baylor {UE,LE} Rehab Program Template.{docx,md}`; text\nextracted by `staging/rtp/docx_to_md.py`. The originals are only in Downloads; the LE file\nname there has a stray space before `.docx`. Both should move to Drive.)\n\nWhat the templates contain: six phases (Healing, Foundation, Reconstruction, Reintegration,\nEvaluation, Competition), each with a primary and secondary owner, training blocks and weekly\nplans, a milestone checklist, and a testing appendix. LE gates: HHD LSI, IMTP, hop battery at\n80% then 90%, CMJ, drop jump, SLJ, 10-yard sprint, 10-5 COD, workload 100%. UE gates: HHD LSI\n90%, ASH test 90%, upper-quarter Y-balance 85%, plyo push-up, throwing progression, workload\n80% then 100%. Applied Performance-relevant owners: S&C is primary from Foundation onward.\n\nThree places the templates sit against the interview (for Eric, not resolved here):\n- **COD (Q13).** \"We don't test change of direction in most sports\", but the LE template gates\n  Evaluation on the 10-5 COD test and lists pro agility and a curvilinear sprint. Reading:\n  COD is tested inside RTP, not in routine team testing.\n- **Movement screens (Q12).** \"Nothing changes decisions\", but both templates gate Foundation\n  on FMS > 14.\n- **Readiness (Q22).** \"We don't assess readiness. The template answers that.\" The template's\n  Evaluation phase is in effect a readiness gate (outputs, workload 100%, subjective\n  questionnaire, physician clearance), so the answer is better read as \"readiness is decided\n  by these criteria, not by a separate daily assessment\"."}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CfWHeMmYgbvC2GjTgvW8G","type":"assistant","uuid":"ce71c531-6a8f-4142-afb2-26d402206865","timestamp":"2026-09-28T18:11:06.270Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"e054b45d-33cd-4562-af51-7c3370696c58","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\Flint\\.claude\\worktrees\\step1-triage","sessionId":"e054b45d-33cd-4562-af51-7c3370696c58","version":"2.1.283","gitBranch":"step1-triage"}
{"parentUuid":"ce71c531-6a8f-4142-afb2-26d402206865","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"2876ffd3-8d74-4539-a14c-a9a62bf4476e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MoMZ4XuxocM1BA2rPx3P9r","type":"tool_result","content":"The file C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\Flint\\.claude\\worktrees\\step1-triage\\docs\\interview\\2026-09-28-method-interview.md has been updated successfully."}]},"uuid":"7e13010c-a73d-458b-809f-2fa3d4d60114","timestamp":"2026-09-28T18:11:06.496Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\Flint\\.claude\\worktrees\\step1-triage\\docs\\interview\\2026-09-28-method-interview.md","oldString":"(Not yet staged. Next step: copy both to Drive and stage a text copy for the RTP synthesis.)","newString":"(Staged 2026-09-28 as `staging/rtp/Baylor {UE,LE} Rehab Program Template.{docx,md}`; text\nextracted by `staging/rtp/docx_to_md.py`. The originals are only in Downloads; the LE file\nname there has a stray space before `.docx`. Both should move to Drive.)\n\nWhat the templates contain: six phases (Healing, Foundation, Reconstruction, Reintegration,\nEvaluation, Competition), each with a primary and secondary owner, training blocks and weekly\nplans, a milestone checklist, and a testing appendix. LE gates: HHD LSI, IMTP, hop battery at\n80% then 90%, CMJ, drop jump, SLJ, 10-yard sprint, 10-5 COD, workload 100%. UE gates: HHD LSI\n90%, ASH test 90%, upper-quarter Y-balance 85%, plyo push-up, throwing progression, workload\n80% then 100%. Applied Performance-relevant owners: S&C is primary from Foundation onward.\n\nThree places the templates sit against the interview (for Eric, not resolved here):\n- **COD (Q13).** \"We don't test change of direction in most sports\", but the LE template gates\n  Evaluation on the 10-5 COD test and lists pro agility and a curvilinear sprint. Reading:\n  COD is tested inside RTP, not in routine team testing.\n- **Movement screens (Q12).** \"Nothing changes decisions\", but both templates gate Foundation\n  on FMS > 14.\n- **Readiness (Q22).** \"We don't assess readiness. The template answers that.\" The template's\n  Evaluation phase is in effect a readiness gate (outputs, workload 100%, subjective\n  questionnaire, physician clearance), so the answer is better read as \"readiness is decided\n  by these criteria, not by a separate daily assessment\".","originalFile":null,"structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":45,"oldLines":8,"newStart":45,"newLines":28,"lines":[" > `C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Downloads\\Baylor UE Rehab Program Template.docx` and"," > `C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Downloads\\Baylor LE Rehab Program Template.docx`"," ","-(Not yet staged. Next step: copy both to Drive and stage a text copy for the RTP synthesis.)","+(Staged 2026-09-28 as `staging/rtp/Baylor {UE,LE} Rehab Program Template.{docx,md}`; text","+extracted by `staging/rtp/docx_to_md.py`. The originals are only in Downloads; the LE file","+name there has a stray space before `.docx`. Both should move to Drive.)"," ","+What the templates contain: six phases (Healing, Foundation, Reconstruction, Reintegration,","+Evaluation, Competition), each with a primary and secondary owner, training blocks and weekly","+plans, a milestone checklist, and a testing appendix. LE gates: HHD LSI, IMTP, hop battery at","+80% then 90%, CMJ, drop jump, SLJ, 10-yard sprint, 10-5 COD, workload 100%. UE gates: HHD LSI","+90%, ASH test 90%, upper-quarter Y-balance 85%, plyo push-up, throwing progression, workload","+80% then 100%. Applied Performance-relevant owners: S&C is primary from Foundation onward.","+","+Three places the templates sit against the interview (for Eric, not resolved here):","+- **COD (Q13).** \"We don't test change of direction in most sports\", but the LE template gates","+  Evaluation on the 10-5 COD test and lists pro agility and a curvilinear sprint. Reading:","+  COD is tested inside RTP, not in routine team testing.","+- **Movement screens (Q12).** \"Nothing changes decisions\", but both templates gate Foundation","+  on FMS > 14.","+- **Readiness (Q22).** \"We don't assess readiness. The template answers that.\" The template's","+  Evaluation phase is in effect a readiness gate (outputs, workload 100%, subjective","+  questionnaire, physician clearance), so the answer is better read as \"readiness is decided","+  by these criteria, not by a separate daily assessment\".","+"," ## Round 2: testing, force plate, load"," "," **7. GPS and load thresholds per sport.** Do any exist informally?"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false,"contentNotInModelContext":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ce71c531-6a8f-4142-afb2-26d402206865","session_id":"e054b45d-33cd-4562-af51-7c3370696c58","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\Flint\\.claude\\worktrees\\step1-triage","sessionId":"e054b45d-33cd-4562-af51-7c3370696c58","version":"2.1.283","gitBranch":"step1-triage"}
