thlete rollup; `Football/SpringPlayerEvals_SymAnalysis`\n405:  Zotero labels, so not a reuse); (3) spring exit notes, judged against the Claude pass\n406:  (rho 0.30, n 34), never by fitting weights; (4) Fireflies meeting to project, only if\n# Jev capability map\n\nWhat TypeSafe's System One model (Jev) can and cannot do, and where it fits the work\nwe already run. Written 2026-09-19 after reading the full doc set. The vendor mirror in\n`docs/vendor/typesafe/` is the reference; this file is the judgment.\n\n| Legacy Office format (.doc, .ppt) | 3 |\n| Encrypted PDF | 1 |\n| PDF parser limit | 1 |\n\nSo 87 of 200 files carry no first-page text. That is thinner than the pre-registration\nassumed, but identical for every model and for the answer key.\n\nMethod notes:\n- All documents were fetched by Drive id with `gws`, one method for every root.\n- There is no Anthropic API key on this machine. Haiku runs through headless\n  `claude -p --model claude-haiku-4-5`, one call per file with the same state and the same\n  forced topic.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"34d8237c-9785-4de4-bbd7-bd3db362bfc1","timestamp":"2026-09-28T18:11:26.162Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"{\"sample_id\": \"S001\", \"topic\": \"filename-or-placeholder-title\", \"domain\": \"not-a-research-record\", \"confidence\": 0.99, \"top\": [[\"filename-or-placeholder-title\", 1.0], [\"data-governance-privacy-and-ethics\", 0.0], [\"concussion-and-head-injury\", 0.0], [\"return-to-play-criteria-and-progression\", 0.0], [\"aerobic-and-anaerobic-capacity-testing\", 0.0]], \"route\": \"a research paper\", \"route_confidence\": 0.\n51:| Latency | About 100 to 115 ms per call, measured across two cookbooks |\n70:   one measured pair summed to 1.19. Never carry a threshold tuned on one primitive\n163:measured, and there is no problem here to solve.** ~~We have the same name spelled four\n181:>   Measured on Baylor's data the split is 96%/4%, and the 96% needs no model —\n225:about 4k tokens, so our ~155 fit inside the 32k budget with room to spare. Measured on\n250:`entity_alignment` (**withdrawn**, measured) and PP_Recruiting screening (**rejected**).\n254:Every item that was measured moved, and every one moved *down*. Entity alignment was\n257:at the cookbook's 0.90 and measured to 0.80; the Zotero cutoff came in at 0.90 and\n258:measured to 0.50. That is not bad luck, it is a missing gate. **Build only where all\n264:3. **A code baseline was measured first.** If deterministic code gets most of the way,\n271:band was measured before and after.\n277:with Jev on 5 of 8 rules-picks), and the spring notes (role words the labels missed).\n307:> decision holds on the measured share and under either adversarial bound alone, on\n348:> item measured off the map. Write-up: `docs/RERANK_MEASUREMENT.md`.\n350:**2. `rerank_typesafe` — second because it is the one that can be measured cheaply.**\n398:  the annual report and the 534-athlete rollup; `Football/SpringPlayerEvals_SymAnalysis`\n405:  Zotero labels, so not a reuse); (3) spring exit notes, judged against the Claude pass\n406:  (rho 0.30, n 34), never by fitting weights; (4) Fireflies meeting to project, only if\n# Jev capability map\n\nWhat TypeSafe's System One model (Jev) can and cannot do, and where it fits the work\nwe already run. Written 2026-09-19 after reading the full doc set. The vendor mirror in\n`docs/vendor/typesafe/` is the reference; this file is the judgment.\n\n| Legacy Office format (.doc, .ppt) | 3 |\n| Encrypted PDF | 1 |\n| PDF parser limit | 1 |\n\nSo 87 of 200 files carry no first-page text. That is thinner than the pre-registration\nassumed, but identical for every model and for the answer key.\n\nMethod notes:\n- All documents were fetched by Drive id with `gws`, one method for every root.\n- There is no Anthropic API key on this machine. Haiku runs through headless\n  `claude -p --model claude-haiku-4-5`, one call per file with the same state and the same\n  forced topic.","stderr":"","interrupted":false