{"parentUuid":"15c7510c-b409-4f40-9163-602f3849b53b","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"2876ffd3-8d74-4539-a14c-a9a62bf4476e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017XhJxVjhNLWF2rpVpHbUxS","type":"tool_result","content":"**`function_calling`** reads better on the map than it is. Claude Code already *is*\nthe natural-language-to-CLI layer, so routing a chat request through Jev adds a step\nwhere a working one exists. The one place it is not redundant is the same place the\nskill router paid off: **as a hook**, deciding without a conversation turn. Build it\nonly in that form, or not at all.\n\n## Re-ranked 2026-09-21, after a sweep of every project\n\nFull ranking, kill tests and coverage: `docs/handoffs/2026-09-21-leverage-sweep-all-projects.md`.\n\n- **Text-to-features is no longer blocked on a corpus.** `Ath_Medicine` holds 7,555\n  medical diagnostics notes (3,924 cleaned) already read by six regex/TF-IDF scripts feeding\n  the annual report and the 534-athlete rollup; `Football/SpringPlayerEvals_SymAnalysis`\n  holds 99 x 4 department notes behind the Coach One-Pager. The closeout's \"one access\n  conversation unblocks two items\" now holds for neither (`semantic_find` had no real\n  target; see the 2026-09-25 correction above).\n- **New order:** (1) Ath_Medicine notes, surgery tagger first, gated on Eric extending\n  Option C to clinical note text; (2) Evidence Library domain tags, the only item with a\n  ready labelled set (300 reviewed; regex exact-set 55/300; only 151/707 overlap the\n  Zotero labels, so not a reuse); (3) spring exit notes, judged against the Claude pass\n  (rho 0.30, n 34), never by fitting weights; (4) Fireflies meeting to project, only if\n  an attendee lookup settles under 80%; (5) Tech Inventory athlete-data screening, the\n  one item on the slate; (6) matchup injury triage, where the fetch is the real work.\n- **`rerank_typesafe`:** no transcript evidence of misses (14 memsearch mentions, all\n  infrastructure). Its pre-registered measurement is running in another worktree; that\n  result decides its rank, not this sweep.\n\n['confidence', 'domain', 'ms', 'route', 'route_confidence', 'sample_id', 'top', 'topic']\r\nms 56432","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"509bba2e-f7c9-4dbb-b89d-433383fa741f","timestamp":"2026-09-28T18:11:31.036Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"**`function_calling`** reads better on the map than it is. Claude Code already *is*\nthe natural-language-to-CLI layer, so routing a chat request through Jev adds a step\nwhere a working one exists. The one place it is not redundant is the same place the\nskill router paid off: **as a hook**, deciding without a conversation turn. Build it\nonly in that form, or not at all.\n\n## Re-ranked 2026-09-21, after a sweep of every project\n\nFull ranking, kill tests and coverage: `docs/handoffs/2026-09-21-leverage-sweep-all-projects.md`.\n\n- **Text-to-features is no longer blocked on a corpus.** `Ath_Medicine` holds 7,555\n  medical diagnostics notes (3,924 cleaned) already read by six regex/TF-IDF scripts feeding\n  the annual report and the 534-athlete rollup; `Football/SpringPlayerEvals_SymAnalysis`\n  holds 99 x 4 department notes behind the Coach One-Pager. The closeout's \"one access\n  conversation unblocks two items\" now holds for neither (`semantic_find` had no real\n  target; see the 2026-09-25 correction above).\n- **New order:** (1) Ath_Medicine notes, surgery tagger first, gated on Eric extending\n  Option C to clinical note text; (2) Evidence Library domain tags, the only item with a\n  ready labelled set (300 reviewed; regex exact-set 55/300; only 151/707 overlap the\n  Zotero labels, so not a reuse); (3) spring exit notes, judged against the Claude pass\n  (rho 0.30, n 34), never by fitting weights; (4) Fireflies meeting to project, only if\n  an attendee lookup settles under 80%; (5) Tech Inventory athlete-data screening, the\n  one item on the slate; (6) matchup injury triage, where the fetch is the real work.\n- **`rerank_typesafe`:** no transcript evidence of misses (14 memsearch mentions, all\n  infrastructure). Its pre-registered measurement is running in another worktree; that\n  result decides its rank, not this sweep.\n\n['confidence', 'domain', 'ms', 'route', 'route_confidence', 'sample_id', 'top', 'topic']\r\nms 56432","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"15c7510c-b409-4f40-9163-602f3849b53b","session_id":"e054b45d-33cd-4562-af51-7c3370696c58","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\TypeSafe_Sandbox\\.claude\\worktrees\\drive-triage-run","sessionId":"e054b45d-33cd-4562-af51-7c3370696c58","version":"2.1.283","gitBranch":"worktree-drive-triage-run"}
