{"parentUuid":"0ec6079d-52a1-47b9-a967-5266d879d700","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfWHh2BfC74GhyYbtHG9U","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TQUgsiZB25TqCSzgCQoHV2","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\TypeSafe_Sandbox\\.claude\\worktrees\\drive-triage-run\\docs\\STATUS.md","old_string":"- **2026-09-26 (Drive triage, REGISTERED, not run)**: tenth measurement. Can Jev place the Drive files Flint's keyword rules miss (3,548 of 9,712) into the Zotero taxonomy? Pre-registered in `docs/DRIVE_TRIAGE_PREREG.md` with the 200-file sample (`drive_triage/sample.csv`, seed 20260926). Bars were approved by Eric before any call: confident on at least 60%, domain accuracy at least 90% on the confident answers, and at least equal to Haiku. Next: build the state, then Claude's blind answer key, committed before the first Jev call. Consumer: `erash11/Flint`.","new_string":"- **2026-09-28 (Drive triage, SCORED: FAILS on one bar; Eric chose Jev anyway)**: tenth\n  measurement, pre-registered in `docs/DRIVE_TRIAGE_PREREG.md`. On the original labels Jev was\n  **confident on 166/200 (83%, bar 60%: pass)**, but **right on the domain for 127/166 (76.5%,\n  bar 90%: FAIL)**. **Jev beat Haiku** on its confident subset (127 vs 108: pass) and on every\n  unbarred measure: domain on all 200 was 74.5% vs 66.0%, topic 63.5% vs 52.0%, route 66.5% vs\n  63.0%. On the unclassified half, which is Flint's real target, Jev's confident answers were\n  right on 69/81 (85.2%). On the rules-classified half they were right on only 58/85 (68.2%);\n  the rules themselves scored 52/100. Thin state hurt: 87 files have no first-page text, and\n  Jev was right on 50 of the 77 of those it was confident on. The prereg's fail branch (\"the\n  best comparator does the pass\") assumed a comparator would beat Jev, and none did. **Eric's\n  decision (2026-09-28): Jev does Flint's pass**, keeping his shortlist approval step because\n  about 1 in 4 confident domains are wrong. The verdict stays FAIL. **Codex comparator:**\n  98/200, paused twice by low memory (a recurring 2.6 GB memsearch reindex). **Audit:** the blind\n  sheet (`drive_triage/private/audit_sheet.md`, 20 of 39 confident disagreements) is waiting on\n  Eric; its score is reported next to the original and never changes the verdict. Results:\n  `drive_triage/results.md`."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1075,"cache_read_input_tokens":211747,"output_tokens":1325,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":319},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1075,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1325,"cache_read_input_tokens":211747,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1075,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1075},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01TQUgsiZB25TqCSzgCQoHV2":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\TypeSafe_Sandbox\\.claude\\worktrees\\drive-triage-run\\docs\\STATUS.md","old_string":"- **2026-09-26 (Drive triage, REGISTERED, not run)**: tenth measurement. Can Jev place the Drive files Flint's keyword rules miss (3,548 of 9,712) into the Zotero taxonomy? Pre-registered in `docs/DRIVE_TRIAGE_PREREG.md` with the 200-file sample (`drive_triage/sample.csv`, seed 20260926). Bars were approved by Eric before any call: confident on at least 60%, domain accuracy at least 90% on the confident answers, and at least equal to Haiku. Next: build the state, then Claude's blind answer key, committed before the first Jev call. Consumer: `erash11/Flint`.","new_string":"- **2026-09-28 (Drive triage, SCORED: FAILS on one bar; Eric chose Jev anyway)**: tenth\n  measurement, pre-registered in `docs/DRIVE_TRIAGE_PREREG.md`. On the original labels Jev was\n  **confident on 166/200 (83%, bar 60%: pass)**, but **right on the domain for 127/166 (76.5%,\n  bar 90%: FAIL)**. **Jev beat Haiku** on its confident subset (127 vs 108: pass) and on every\n  unbarred measure: domain on all 200 was 74.5% vs 66.0%, topic 63.5% vs 52.0%, route 66.5% vs\n  63.0%. On the unclassified half, which is Flint's real target, Jev's confident answers were\n  right on 69/81 (85.2%). On the rules-classified half they were right on only 58/85 (68.2%);\n  the rules themselves scored 52/100. Thin state hurt: 87 files have no first-page text, and\n  Jev was right on 50 of the 77 of those it was confident on. The prereg's fail branch (\"the\n  best comparator does the pass\") assumed a comparator would beat Jev, and none did. **Eric's\n  decision (2026-09-28): Jev does Flint's pass**, keeping his shortlist approval step because\n  about 1 in 4 confident domains are wrong. The verdict stays FAIL. **Codex comparator:**\n  98/200, paused twice by low memory (a recurring 2.6 GB memsearch reindex). **Audit:** the blind\n  sheet (`drive_triage/private/audit_sheet.md`, 20 of 39 confident disagreements) is waiting on\n  Eric; its score is reported next to the original and never changes the verdict. Results:\n  `drive_triage/results.md`."}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfWHh1eQZcCVHo43mSn9h","type":"assistant","uuid":"b3d85901-ce23-483b-bbdf-b7b86c01640e","timestamp":"2026-09-28T18:11:43.384Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"e054b45d-33cd-4562-af51-7c3370696c58","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\TypeSafe_Sandbox\\.claude\\worktrees\\drive-triage-run","sessionId":"e054b45d-33cd-4562-af51-7c3370696c58","version":"2.1.28