{"parentUuid":"0fbd7523-7210-4e9c-b29b-6040d81a82f2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfWHhzcRKvnpvb3UjwqbX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01W15A5iKZRMPS7v29pVWydi","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\TypeSafe_Sandbox\\.claude\\worktrees\\drive-triage-run\\docs\\JEV_CAPABILITY_MAP.md","old_string":"## Re-ranked 2026-09-21, after a sweep of every project","new_string":"## Drive triage, the tenth measurement (scored 2026-09-28): FAIL, used anyway\n\nPre-registration: `docs/DRIVE_TRIAGE_PREREG.md`. Results: `drive_triage/results.md`.\n\n| Bar | Needed | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| Confident (p >= 0.50) | 60% of 200 | 166/200 (83%): pass |\n| Domain accuracy, confident answers | 90% | 127/166 (76.5%): **fail** |\n| Jev vs Haiku, same subset | Jev >= Haiku | 127 vs 108: pass |\n\n- **Jev won every comparison and still missed the absolute bar.** On all 200 it beat Haiku on\n  domain (74.5% vs 66.0%) and topic (63.5% vs 52.0%). Codex stopped at 98/200 (memory), so it\n  is not scored.\n- **Where it held up:** the files the keyword rules could not place, which is the population\n  Flint actually needs. There Jev's confident answers were right on 85.2% (69/81). On files the\n  rules had already placed, it was right on only 68.2%.\n- **What hurt:** the state. 87 of 200 files had no first-page text (video, scans, empty Drive\n  entries). A file name and a folder cannot carry a 90% bar.\n- **Decision (Eric, 2026-09-28):** Jev does Flint's pass, with Eric's shortlist approval kept\n  as the check. The verdict stays FAIL, and this is not a rescue under the audit rule.\n\n**The lesson for the next pre-registration.** The fail branch said \"the best comparator does\nthe pass\". It never said what happens when the model fails its bar but beats every\ncomparator. That left a decision to be made after the results, which is exactly what\npre-registration exists to prevent. Every future prereg states both branches before the\nfirst call: (a) fails the bar and loses to a comparator, then the comparator runs; (b) fails\nthe bar but beats every comparator, then name in advance whether the model runs with a human\ncheck, or nothing runs.\n\n## Re-ranked 2026-09-21, after a sweep of every project"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1424,"cache_read_input_tokens":212822,"output_tokens":1100,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":197},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1424,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1100,"cache_read_input_tokens":212822,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1424,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1424},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01W15A5iKZRMPS7v29pVWydi":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\TypeSafe_Sandbox\\.claude\\worktrees\\drive-triage-run\\docs\\JEV_CAPABILITY_MAP.md","old_string":"## Re-ranked 2026-09-21, after a sweep of every project","new_string":"## Drive triage, the tenth measurement (scored 2026-09-28): FAIL, used anyway\n\nPre-registration: `docs/DRIVE_TRIAGE_PREREG.md`. Results: `drive_triage/results.md`.\n\n| Bar | Needed | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| Confident (p >= 0.50) | 60% of 200 | 166/200 (83%): pass |\n| Domain accuracy, confident answers | 90% | 127/166 (76.5%): **fail** |\n| Jev vs Haiku, same subset | Jev >= Haiku | 127 vs 108: pass |\n\n- **Jev won every comparison and still missed the absolute bar.** On all 200 it beat Haiku on\n  domain (74.5% vs 66.0%) and topic (63.5% vs 52.0%). Codex stopped at 98/200 (memory), so it\n  is not scored.\n- **Where it held up:** the files the keyword rules could not place, which is the population\n  Flint actually needs. There Jev's confident answers were right on 85.2% (69/81). On files the\n  rules had already placed, it was right on only 68.2%.\n- **What hurt:** the state. 87 of 200 files had no first-page text (video, scans, empty Drive\n  entries). A file name and a folder cannot carry a 90% bar.\n- **Decision (Eric, 2026-09-28):** Jev does Flint's pass, with Eric's shortlist approval kept\n  as the check. The verdict stays FAIL, and this is not a rescue under the audit rule.\n\n**The lesson for the next pre-registration.** The fail branch said \"the best comparator does\nthe pass\". It never said what happens when the model fails its bar but beats every\ncomparator. That left a decision to be made after the results, which is exactly what\npre-registration exists to prevent. Every future prereg states both branches before the\nfirst call: (a) fails the bar and loses to a comparator, then the comparator runs; (b) fails\nthe bar but beats every comparator, then name in advance whether the model runs with a human\ncheck, or nothing runs.\n\n## Re-ranked 2026-09-21, after a sweep of every project"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfWHhz7QfJNpuH47dVfV9","type":"assistant","uuid":"c23f1a1b-9601-4ec5-b64d-d80cd071ba97","timestamp":"2026-09-28T18:11:54.701Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"e054b45d-33cd-4562-af51-7c3370696c58","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\TypeSafe_Sandbox\\.claude\\worktrees\\drive-triage-run","sessionId":"e054b45d-33cd-4562-af51-7c3370696c58","version":"2.1.283","gitBranch":"worktree-drive-triage-run"}
