{"parentUuid":"71937422-6c92-4f3e-bfc9-377dc711c6ff","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfWHipEsKTodFWNR8uUYS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FfsSW6rSCddJdb9CXLAX3A","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat >> drive_triage/README.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Result (2026-09-28)\n\nScored with `score.py`; the full table is in `results.md`. Verdict on the original labels:\n**FAIL** (confident 83%: pass; domain accuracy on confident answers 76.5% against a 90% bar:\nfail; Jev 127 vs Haiku 108 on the same subset: pass). Eric chose Jev for Flint's pass anyway,\nwith his shortlist approval kept as the check (`docs/JEV_CAPABILITY_MAP.md`, tenth measurement).\n\n- Haiku: 200/200, 0 parse failures, about 35-60 s per call via headless `claude -p`.\n- Codex: 98/200. The run was stopped twice by Claude Code's low-memory reaper, and it resumes\n  from `runs/codex.jsonl`.\n- Cost: `run_jev.py` records latency only (56.4 s total over 200 calls), not credits, so the\n  cost line the prereg asks for is latency plus call count.\n- Audit: `private/audit_sheet.md` (20 of 39 confident disagreements) is waiting on Eric.\nEOF\ngit add docs/STATUS.md docs/JEV_CAPABILITY_MAP.md drive_triage/README.md drive_triage/results.md && git commit -q -m \"drive_triage: write up the tenth measurement (FAIL on domain accuracy; Jev beats Haiku; Eric chooses Jev for Flint)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tr551YYoFPCB1DSy2iUtz5\" && git push -q && git log --oneline -1","description":"Add result to README, commit and push write-up"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1210,"cache_read_input_tokens":214246,"output_tokens":679,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fet