{"parentUuid":"7bfa2037-2d0e-445b-abcd-0f872cc62aa5","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"5ab30ef3-9175-4097-b2d1-66be52d5c48a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017G3abgjbXypFpY3aPXgXL9","type":"tool_result","content":"d6fb653 drive_triage: Codex comparator complete (200/200); re-scored; Jev stays the choice","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"a0a8d185-7520-490a-ada6-f77dc0ae8eda","timestamp":"2026-09-28T19:25:20.438Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"d6fb653 drive_triage: Codex comparator complete (200/200); re-scored; Jev stays the choice","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\TypeSafe_Sandbox\\.claude\\worktrees\\drive-triage-run\\docs\\JEV_CAPABILITY_MAP.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":400,"oldLines":8,"newStart":400,"newLines":8,"lines":[" | Jev vs Haiku, same subset | Jev >= Haiku | 127 vs 108: pass |\r"," \r"," - **Jev won every comparison and still missed the absolute bar.** On all 200 it beat Haiku on\r","-  domain (74.5% vs 66.0%) and topic (63.5% vs 52.0%). Codex stopped at 98/200 (memory), so it\r","-  is not scored.\r","+  domain (74.5% vs 66.0%) and topic (63.5% vs 52.0%). Codex (200/200) tied it on domain\r","+  (148 vs 149) but was worse on the unclassified half (75 vs 81) and has no confidence signal.\r"," - **Where it held up:** the files the keyword rules could not place, which is the population\r","   Flint actually needs. There Jev's confident answers were right on 85.2% (69/81). On files the\r","   rules had already placed, it was right on only 68.2%.\r"]}]},{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\TypeSafe_Sandbox\\.claude\\worktrees\\drive-triage-run\\docs\\STATUS.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":14,"oldLines":8,"newStart":14,"newLines":7,"lines":["   Jev was right on 50 of the 77 of those it was confident on. The prereg's fail branch (\"the\r","   best comparator does the pass\") assumed a comparator would beat Jev, and none did. **Eric's\r","   decision (2026-09-28): Jev does Flint's pass**, keeping his shortlist approval step because\r","-  about 1 in 4 confident domains are wrong. The verdict stays FAIL. **Codex comparator:**\r","-  98/200, paused twice by low memory (a recurring 2.6 GB memsearch reindex). **Audit:** the blind\r","+  about 1 in 4 confident domains are wrong. The verdict stays FAIL. **Codex comparator (200/200, 0 failures):** it tied Jev on domain over all 200 (148 vs 149) and edged it on Jev's confident subset (131 vs 127), topic (66.0% vs 63.5%) and route (72.0% vs 66.5%). But on the unclassified half, Flint's target, it was worse (75 vs 81 of 100; 65 vs 69 on Jev's confident 81). It has no confidence signal and takes about 70 s per file against Jev's 0.3 s, so Jev stays the choice. **Audit:** the blind\r","   sheet (`drive_triage/private/audit_sheet.md`, 20 of 39 confident disagreements) is waiting on\r","   Eric; its score is reported next to the original and never changes the verdict. Results:\r","   `drive_triage/results.md`.\r"]}]},{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\TypeSafe_Sandbox\\.claude\\worktrees\\drive-triage-run\\drive_triage\\README.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":53,"newStart":1,"newLines":53,"lines":["-# Drive triage: the Jev pilot (run record)","-","-Pre-registration: `docs/DRIVE_TRIAGE_PREREG.md` (bars fixed 2026-09-26, before any call).","-Sample: `sample.csv` (200 files, seed 20260926).","-","-## Order of work (each step committed before the next)","-","-1. `build_state.py`: state for all 200, built by code. Written to `private/state.jsonl`","-   (gitignored: first-page text of Drive documents).","-   **state.jsonl sha256 `779d3ff481960373070214bda7bdfa4079abd68fed20a7f57a3956c99c06aada`**","-2. `answer_key.csv`: Claude's labels (topic, derived domain, route) for all 200. They were written by one","-   fresh agent that read only `private/state.jsonl` and `taxonomy_for_key.md`. It saw no Flint","-   label, no `sample.csv` column beyond what the state carries, and no model answer.","-   It was committed and pushed before the first Jev call.","-3. `run_jev.py`: Jev, one request per file (topic Choice unchanged from `classify.question()`","-   plus the route Choice defined in the script). Raw answers in `runs/jev.jsonl`.","-4. Comparators (Haiku, Codex) and scoring against the bars.","-","-## State as built (2026-09-28)","-","-| Extraction | Files |","-|---|---:|","-| First page (median about 1,870 characters) | 113 |","-| Path and name only (video, audio, data files; by design) | 53 |","-| PDF with no text layer (scans) | 18 |","-| Empty in Drive (size 0; the Drive entry holds no content) | 7 |","-| Not a readable PDF (3 macOS `._` resource forks, 1 damaged file) | 4 |","-| Legacy Office format (.doc, .ppt) | 3 |","-| Encrypted PDF | 1 |","-| PDF parser limit | 1 |","-","-So 87 of 200 files carry no first-page text. That is thinner than the pre-registration","-assumed, but identical for every model and for the answer key.","-","-Method notes:","-- All documents were fetched by Drive id with `gws`, one method for every root.","-- There is no Anthropic API key on this machine. Haiku runs through headless","-  `claude -p --model claude-haiku-4-5`, one call per file with the same state and the same","-  forced topic.","-","-## Result (2026-09-28)","-","-Scored with `score.py`; the full table is in `results.md`. Verdict on the original labels:","-**FAIL** (confident 83%: pass; domain accuracy on confident answers 76.5% against a 90% bar:","-fail; Jev 127 vs Haiku 108 on the same subset: pass). Eric chose Jev for Flint's pass anyway,","-with his shortlist approval kept as the check (`docs/JEV_CAPABILITY_MAP.md`, tenth measurement).","-","-- Haiku: 200/200, 0 parse failures, about 35-60 s per call via headless `claude -p`.","-- Codex: 98/200. The run was stopped twice by Claude Code's low-memory reaper, and it resumes","-  from `runs/codex.jsonl`.","-- Cost: `run_jev.py` records latency only (56.4 s total over 200 calls), not credits, so the","-  cost line the prereg asks for is latency plus call count.","-- Audit: `private/audit_sheet.md` (20 of 39 confident disagreements) is waiting on Eric.","+# Drive triage: the Jev pilot (run record)\r","+\r","+Pre-registration: `docs/DRIVE_TRIAGE_PREREG.md` (bars fixed 2026-09-26, before any call).\r","+Sample: `sample.csv` (200 files, seed 20260926).\r","+\r","+## Order of work (each step committed before the next)\r","+\r","+1. `build_state.py`: state for all 200, built by code. Written to `private/state.jsonl`\r","+   (gitignored: first-page text of Drive documents).\r","+   **state.jsonl sha256 `779d3ff481960373070214bda7bdfa4079abd68fed20a7f57a3956c99c06aada`**\r","+2. `answer_key.csv`: Claude's labels (topic, derived domain, route) for all 200. They were written by one\r","+   fresh agent that read only `private/state.jsonl` and `taxonomy_for_key.md`. It saw no Flint\r","+   label, no `sample.csv` column beyond what the state carries, and no model answer.\r","+   It was committed and pushed before the first Jev call.\r","+3. `run_jev.py`: Jev, one request per file (topic Choice unchanged from `classify.question()`\r","+   plus the route Choice defined in the script). Raw answers in `runs/jev.jsonl`.\r","+4. Comparators (Haiku, Codex) and scoring against the bars.\r","+\r","+## State as built (2026-09-28)\r","+\r","+| Extraction | Files |\r","+|---|---:|\r","+| First page (median about 1,870 characters) | 113 |\r","+| Path and name only (video, audio, data files; by design) | 53 |\r","+| PDF with no text layer (scans) | 18 |\r","+| Empty in Drive (size 0; the Drive entry holds no content) | 7 |\r","+| Not a readable PDF (3 macOS `._` resource forks, 1 damaged file) | 4 |\r","+| Legacy Office format (.doc, .ppt) | 3 |\r","+| Encrypted PDF | 1 |\r","+| PDF parser limit | 1 |\r","+\r","+So 87 of 200 files carry no first-page text. That is thinner than the pre-registration\r","+assumed, but identical for every model and for the answer key.\r","+\r","+Method notes:\r","+- All documents were fetched by Drive id with `gws`, one method for every root.\r","+- There is no Anthropic API key on this machine. Haiku runs through headless\r","+  `claude -p --model claude-haiku-4-5`, one call per file with the same state and the same\r","+  forced topic.\r","+\r","+## Result (2026-09-28)\r","+\r","+Scored with `score.py`; the full table is in `results.md`. Verdict on the original labels:\r","+**FAIL** (confident 83%: pass; domain accuracy on confident answers 76.5% against a 90% bar:\r","+fail; Jev 127 vs Haiku 108 on the same subset: pass). Eric chose Jev for Flint's pass anyway,\r","+with his shortlist approval kept as the check (`docs/JEV_CAPABILITY_MAP.md`, tenth measurement).\r","+\r","+- Haiku: 200/200, 0 parse failures, about 35-60 s per call via headless `claude -p`.\r","+- Codex: 200/200, 0 failures, about 70 s per call; finished in foreground chunks after the\r","+  low-memory reaper stopped two background runs. it tied Jev on domain over all 200 (148 vs 149) and edged it on Jev's confident subset (131 vs 127), topic (66.0% vs 63.5%) and route (72.0% vs 66.5%). But on the unclassified half, Flint's target, it was worse (75 vs 81 of 100; 65 vs 69 on Jev's confident 81). It has no confidence signal and takes about 70 s per file against Jev's 0.3 s, so Jev stays the choice.\r","+- Cost: `run_jev.py` records latency only (56.4 s total over 200 calls), not credits, so the\r","+  cost line the prereg asks for is latency plus call count.\r","+- Audit: `private/audit_sheet.md` (20 of 39 confident disagreements) is waiting on Eric."]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\TypeSafe_Sandbox\\.claude\\worktrees\\drive-triage-run\\docs\\JEV_CAPABILITY_MAP.md","C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\TypeSafe_Sandbox\\.claude\\worktrees\\drive-triage-run\\docs\\STATUS.md","C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\TypeSafe_Sandbox\\.claude\\worktrees\\drive-triage-run