{"parentUuid":"25019f4e-d369-4bce-833d-2dbc89c3e8e9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfWPN37tB3N1rd9Zg3Haj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Four of the five tasks are done. The fifth, the primer on constraints-led coaching, is being written now.\n\n| # | Task | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Apply your interview answers to the baseline and peaking synthesis rev 3 | ✅ Pushed (`4ac2693`) |\n| 2 | Stage the UE and LE rehab templates | ✅ In `staging/rtp/`, notes pushed (`8a55a84`) |\n| 3 | Write up the Jev pilot and open a draft PR | ✅ [PR #31](https://github.com/erash11/TypeSafe_Sandbox/pull/31), draft |\n| 4 | Codex comparator | ✅ 200/200, re-scored (`d6fb653`) |\n| 5 | Constraints-led coaching primer | ⏳ One subagent is writing it now (3 of 5 used) |\n\n**Codex result: Jev is still the right choice.**\n- **Codex roughly tied Jev on domain** over all 200 files (148 vs 149), and did a bit better on topic and route.\n- **Codex was worse where Flint needs it most.** On the files the keyword rules couldn't place, it got 75 right to Jev's 81.\n- **Codex is too slow and gives no confidence score.** It takes about 70 seconds per file against Jev's 0.3, which works out to roughly 3 days of runtime for Flint's ~3,500 files. And without a confidence score, there's no way to tell which answers need checking.\n\n**Your interview answers conflict with each other or your documents in a few places.** You don't need to resolve these today:\n- **Readiness:** you read mRSI on Wednesdays, but your SportSmith piece describes a daily read. You also said \"we don't assess readiness\".\n- **Your own slides:** two of your answers contradict slides from a class you taught (heart-rate method, and which quality fades first).\n- **Change of direction and movement screens:** you said you don't test COD, but your LE rehab template gates the Evaluation phase on the 10-5 COD test. You said screens change nothing, but both templates gate Foundation on FMS > 14.\n- **1RM loading:** no sport does true 1RM testing, but your course's loading charts are written as percentages of 1RM.\n\n**The primer ties into your RTP constraints-led course.** You said you don't fully understand the constraints-led approach, yet you're building a course around it. So the primer is framed around what you'd need to own that course. Results come when the subagent reports back.\n\n**Still waiting on you:**\n- Approve the Flint shortlists. The Drive catalog re-run is held until then.\n- The blind Jev audit (20 rows).\n- Listen through the 47 flagged spots in the CVASPS transcript.\n- Move your two rehab templates from Downloads to Drive. The LE one has a stray space in its file name."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1903,"cache_read_input_tokens":228427,"output_tokens":947,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1903,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":947,"cache_read_input_tokens":228427,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1903,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1903},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfWPN2ae7Y6KQRVjiaGKn","type":"assistant","uuid":"80e3da8a-37ef-4a37-95a0-5f0a8e2d4cc3","timestamp":"2026-09-28T19:26:04.168Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"e054b45d-33cd-4562-af51-7c3370696c58","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\Flint\\.claude\\worktrees\\step1-triage","sessionId":"e054b45d-33cd-4562-af51-7c3370696c5