{"parentUuid":"b2f9d5e3-056c-4a20-a73d-e461c02c7f73","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfWPxKMeBXhCEYRJLQoyH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All five tasks are done, and everything is committed and pushed: Flint `step1-triage` at `9d8441a`, and TypeSafe draft [PR #31](https://github.com/erash11/TypeSafe_Sandbox/pull/31).\n\n**Task 5, the primer: `Flint/docs/primers/constraints-led-approach.md`.** It draws on 11 papers from your Zotero library and about 17 entries from your vault (Myszka, Harries, Moyer).\n- **The most useful point for you:** in Young 2015, physical qualities explained 57% of pre-planned change-of-direction speed but only 14% of reactive agility. So the Evaluation tests in your LE rehab template (10-yard sprint, 5-10-5) certify speed, not agility. That's a concrete place the constraints-led approach would change your return-to-play protocol.\n- **Evidence gaps:** no constraints-led trial exists in college football or return to play. Much of the support comes from youth-skill studies and single cases, and the primer says so.\n- **Your RTP course:** two of its eight lessons are built. Joe hasn't done the first field task yet. Two sources the course relies on are missing: the Myszka PDF isn't in `sources/`, and the Bobrownicki critique isn't in Zotero. Since Joe's questions go to you, the primer is aimed at what you'd need to own the course.\n- It ends with **three questions for you**, which would turn it into your own position.\n\n**Still waiting on you:**\n1. Approve the Flint shortlists. The Drive catalog re-run is held until you do.\n2. The blind Jev audit: 20 rows in `TypeSafe_Sandbox/.../drive_triage/private/audit_sheet.md`.\n3. Read the primer and answer its three questions.\n4. Listen through the 47 flagged spots in the CVASPS transcript.\n5. Move the two rehab templates from Downloads to Drive.\n\n**Something to fix separately:** the memsearch reindex uses about 2.6 GB and ran twice today. It's what kept stopping the background jobs. Fixing it is worth its own session."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1190,"cache_read_input_tokens":232766,"output_tokens":704,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1190,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":704,"cache_read_input_tokens":232766,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1190,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1190},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfWPxJpPuqHX2NKCrDx8F","type":"assistant","uuid":"7dfabc49-03c9-4b46-8549-b25229a538f8","timestamp":"2026-09-28T19:33:46.427Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"e054b45d-33cd-4562-af51-7c3370696c58","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\Flint\\.claude\\worktrees\\step1-triage","sessionId":"e054b45d-33cd-4562-af51-7c3370696c58","version":"2.1.283","gitBranch":"step1-triage"}
