{"parentUuid":"af8a5fee-8625-4eec-ac17-019beb34ea2e","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_non_blocking_error","hookName":"PreToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_0126tepwFth8MajEHf14B56A","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","stderr":"Failed with non-blocking status code: /usr/bin/bash: line 1: /Users/kristinarash/.local/bin/dcg: No such file or directory","stdout":"","exitCode":127,"command":"/Users/kristinarash/.local/bin/dcg","durationMs":79},"type":"attachment","uuid":"ded04913-d3f1-4f86-8cb7-6022fecd806d","timestamp":"2026-09-28T20:23:16.742Z","session_id":"e054b45d-33cd-4562-af51-7c3370696c58","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\Flint\\.claude\\worktrees\\step1-triage","sessionId":"e054b45d-33cd-4562-af51-7c3370696c58","version":"2.1.283","gitBranch":"step1-triage"}
{"parentUuid":"af8a5fee-8625-4eec-ac17-019beb34ea2e","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"28ec5541-f125-4afa-94de-6e3e5c2897ff","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0126tepwFth8MajEHf14B56A","type":"tool_result","content":"README.md\nanatomy-physiology-and-biomechanics.md\ncoaching-skill-acquisition-and-constraints-led-approach.md\nconditioning-and-energy-systems.md\ndata-technology-and-reporting.md\ninjury-risk-and-prevention.md\nleadership-culture-and-psychology.md\nload-monitoring-and-gps.md\nnutrition-and-body-composition.md\nperiodization-and-programming.md\nrecovery-and-sleep.md\nrehab-and-return-to-play.md\nspeed-and-sprint.md\nstrength-and-power.md\ntesting-and-assessment.md\n# Tier-A shortlists (draft, Phase 2)\r\n\r\nThese are the deep-ingest candidates from the Drive triage, one file per discipline. They are\r\ndrafts: nothing here is approved until Eric says so (PLAN Phase 2, last box).\r\n\r\n## How they were made\r\n\r\n1. `scripts/triage_rules.py`: keyword rules classified 5,693 of 9,702 non-own files. The 3,998\r\n   left over are `data/unclassified.csv`.\r\n2. `scripts/triage_model_pass.py`: enriched those from the June Zotero import logs, ran extra\r\n   keyword and skip rules, then applied Claude's labels (`config/model_labels/batch_*.csv`,\r\n   committed). A label with `candidate=yes` makes the file tier A.\r\n3. An independent reviewer tried to falsify every tier-A label and a random 100 of the skips\r\n   (seed 20260927); its changes were applied as label edits. See the handoff\r\n   `docs/handoffs/2026-09-28-flint-triage.md` for the review record.\r\n4. `scripts/build_shortlists.py`: groups tier A by first discipline and writes these files.\r\n\r\nTier A covers only the files the keyword rules could not place. The 5,693 rule-classified\r\nfiles carry no tier. Sources already in `docs/QUEUE.md` or the vault (Supertraining,\r\nBondarchuk, Issurin, Zatsiorsky, Francis, Verkhoshansky, Harries, Old Bull, Landon Evans) stay on\r\nthe lists with Queue = yes, so they are not scheduled twice. Athlete data and Eric's own\r\nmaterial never appear.\r\n\r\nThe review files (`zz_review_*.csv` in `config/model_labels/`) override the batch labels; the\r\n\"Review note\" column shows why a label changed.\r\n\r\nTo change a shortlist, edit the file's row in `config/model_labels/`, then run\r\n`uv run scripts/triage_model_pass.py` and `uv run scripts/build_shortlists.py`.\r\n\r\n## Totals\r\n\r\n<!-- TOTALS:START (generated by scripts/build_shortlists.py) -->\r\n\r\nFiles in the model pass: 3998. Tier A 97, B 2363, C 1538.\r\n\r\n### All files by route\r\n\r\n| Route | Files | Tier A |\r\n|---|---:|---:|\r\n| skip | 1538 | 0 |\r\n| catalog only | 684 | 0 |\r\n| atomize | 683 | 40 |\r\n| already in Zotero | 293 | 3 |\r\n| paper to Zotero | 264 | 0 |\r\n| own material (Phase 1 second pass) | 260 | 0 |\r\n| book | 217 | 33 |\r\n| transcribe | 59 | 21 |\r\n\r\n### Shortlists\r\n\r\n| Discipline | Files | Book | Atomize | Transcribe | Paper | In Zotero | Catalog |\r\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\r\n| [Strength and power](strength-and-power.md) | 27 | 14 | 11 | 2 | 0 | 0 | 0 |\r\n| [Periodization and programming](periodization-and-programming.md) | 17 | 6 | 9 | 2 | 0 | 0 | 0 |\r\n| [Coaching, skill acquisition and constraints-led approach](coaching-skill-acquisition-and-constraints-led-approach.md) | 13 | 1 | 2 | 10 | 0 | 0 | 0 |\r\n| [Speed and sprint](speed-and-sprint.md) | 10 | 2 | 5 | 2 | 0 | 1 | 0 |\r\n| [Rehab and return to play](rehab-and-return-to-play.md) | 8 | 3 | 4 | 1 | 0 | 0 | 0 |\r\n| [Anatomy, physiology and biomechanics](anatomy-physiology-and-biomechanics.md) | 4 | 2 | 2 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 |\r\n| [Leadership, culture and psychology](leadership-culture-and-psychology.md) | 3 | 1 | 2 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 |\r\n| [Conditioning and energy systems](conditioning-and-energy-systems.md) | 3 | 1 | 1 | 1 | 0 | 0 | 0 |","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"531d08aa-f1d5-4f99-a234-90e8cea9cc77","timestamp":"2026-09-28T20:23:17.469Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"README.md\nanatomy-physiology-and-biomechanics.md\ncoaching-skill-acquisition-and-constraints-led-approach.md\nconditioning-and-energy-systems.md\ndata-technology-and-reporting.md\ninjury-risk-and-prevention.md\nleadership-culture-and-psychology.md\nload-monitoring-and-gps.md\nnutrition-and-body-composition.md\nperiodization-and-programming.md\nrecovery-and-sleep.md\nrehab-and-return-to-play.md\nspeed-and-sprint.md\nstrength-and-power.md\ntesting-and-assessment.md\n# Tier-A shortlists (draft, Phase 2)\r\n\r\nThese are the deep-ingest candidates from the Drive triage, one file per discipline. They are\r\ndrafts: nothing here is approved until Eric says so (PLAN Phase 2, last box).\r\n\r\n## How they were made\r\n\r\n1. `scripts/triage_rules.py`: keyword rules classified 5,693 of 9,702 non-own files. The 3,998\r\n   left over are `data/unclassified.csv`.\r\n2. `scripts/triage_model_pass.py`: enriched those from the June Zotero import logs, ran extra\r\n   keyword and skip rules, then applied Claude's labels (`config/model_labels/batch_*.csv`,\r\n   committed). A label with `candidate=yes` makes the file tier A.\r\n3. An independent reviewer tried to falsify every tier-A label and a random 100 of the skips\r\n   (seed 20260927); its changes were applied as label edits. See the handoff\r\n   `docs/handoffs/2026-09-28-flint-triage.md` for the review record.\r\n4. `scripts/build_shortlists.py`: groups tier A by first discipline and writes these files.\r\n\r\nTier A covers only the files the keyword rules could not place. The 5,693 rule-classified\r\nfiles carry no tier. Sources already in `docs/QUEUE.md` or the vault (Supertraining,\r\nBondarchuk, Issurin, Zatsiorsky, Francis, Verkhoshansky, Harries, Old Bull, Landon Evans) stay on\r\nthe lists with Queue = yes, so they are not scheduled twice. Athlete data and Eric's own\r\nmaterial never appear.\r\n\r\nThe review files (`zz_review_*.csv` in `config/model_labe