{"parentUuid":"1582d9db-be12-4f1a-8bd6-58f1d4431506","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfWTrvhh3ojDjA77bjWKi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":803,"cache_read_input_tokens":254784,"output_tokens":2123,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":610},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":803,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2123,"cache_read_input_tokens":254784,"cache_creation_input_tokens":803,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":803},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfWTrv9Cd6zhkF2vcyqvN","type":"assistant","uuid":"29146987-c9d2-4759-bd21-c82dd7db4dbb","timestamp":"2026-09-28T20:25:07.268Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"e054b45d-33cd-4562-af51-7c3370696c58","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\Flint\\.claude\\worktrees\\step1-triage","sessionId":"e054b45d-33cd-4562-af51-7c3370696c58","version":"2.1.283","gitBranch":"step1-triage"}
{"parentUuid":"29146987-c9d2-4759-bd21-c82dd7db4dbb","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfWTrvhh3ojDjA77bjWKi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Answers to your five questions, then the memsearch review.\n\n**1. The shortlists** are in the Flint repo, one file per discipline (14 files, 97 files in total):\n- On GitHub: https://github.com/erash11/Flint/tree/step1-triage/docs/shortlists\n- Locally: `DEV\\Flint\\.claude\\worktrees\\step1-triage\\docs\\shortlists\\`\n\nStart with `README.md`: it has the totals and **the 8 decisions I need from you**. For each file, approve it, cut rows, or say \"approve all\". Once you're done I'll move the approved sources into `QUEUE.md` and re-run the catalog.\n\n**2. The Jev audit** is 20 short items, about 10 minutes. Open `DEV\\TypeSafe_Sandbox\\.claude\\worktrees\\drive-triage-run\\drive_triage\\private\\audit_sheet.md`. It's local only, not on GitHub, because it holds Drive text.\n- Each item shows a file (folder, name, first page) and two domain labels, A and B. You aren't told which one is Jev's.\n- On each `Verdict:` line, write **A**, **B** or **N** (neither), then tell me you're done. I'll score it next to the original result. It can't change the FAIL verdict.\n\n**3. The primer:**\n- On GitHub: https://github.com/erash11/Flint/blob/step1-triage/docs/primers/constraints-led-approach.md\n- Locally: `DEV\\Flint\\.claude\\worktrees\\step1-triage\\docs\\primers\\constraints-led-approach.md`\n\n**4. Yes, there's a timestamp list.** It's section 2 of `docs/cvasps-corroboration-proposals.md` ([GitHub](https://github.com/erash11/Flint/blob/step1-triage/docs/cvasps-corroboration-proposals.md)). Each row gives the timestamp, what the transcript says, the likely intended word, and a confidence level.\n- **Listen to the \"low\" rows first.** Most \"high\" rows are just name spellings, like \"Paff\" for Pfaff or \"Isherin\" for Issurin.\n- The audio is `staging\\audio\\landonevans...wav` in the Flint worktree. The original is in Drive `09_PRO_DEV\\Conference_Materials\\CVASPS`.\n\n**5. The templates are moved**, to Drive `01_PROJECTS\\_ACTIVE\\HighPerformanceInitative_RTP\\Docs\\`. Drive already had older copies from April 15, and today's files differ from them. Nothing was deleted:\n- The April copies were renamed `..._2026-04-15.docx`.\n- Today's versions are now the main `Baylor UE/LE Rehab Program Template.docx`, and the stray space in the LE name is gone.\n- Downloads no longer has either file. The note is committed (`f3c0707`).\n\n---\n\n**The memsearch fix: I'm caught up, and one piece didn't work.**\n\nWhat the other session found and fixed:\n- **The cause:** about 10,100 chunks had never been indexed. This laptop embeds at about 5 seconds per chunk, so each 600-second hook run cleared only about 110 chunks, used up to 3 GB, and was cut off. Headless sessions kept restarting it.\n- **Part of that fan-out was mine.** This morning's Haiku comparator made 200 `claude -p` calls, and each one ended a session.\n- **The fixes, now in place:** the hook skips headless and SDK sessions, runs at most once every 30 minutes, and uses a smaller batch size (peak memory about 0.9 GB instead of 3.1 GB). Codex runs don't trigger the hook, which is why this afternoon's chunks went through cleanly.\n\n**The drain didn't run.** The one-off task meant to clear the backlog (`\\Eric\\memsearch-drain-once`) started at 12:01 and was stopped within about a minute:\n- It exited with code `0xC000013A`, the code for a console being closed or Ctrl+C.\n- It indexed nothing and never wrote its finish line.\n\nSo the backlog is still there. The hook ran again at 12:38 and timed out at 12:48, its 35th timeout in a row. Until the backlog drains, the hook will keep running for 10 minutes each half hour.\n\n**Recommendation: re-run the drain overnight.** At about 5 seconds per chunk it needs roughly 14 hours, at about 0.9 GB, running at low priority. Want me to start it tonight? It's safest with this laptop plugged in and awake."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":803,"cache_read_input_tokens":254784,"output_tokens":2123,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":610},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":803,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2123,"cache_read_input_tokens":254784,"cache_creation_input_tokens":803,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":803},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfWTrv9Cd6zhkF2vcyqvN","type":"assistant","uuid":"5ec8c71d-a6bf-4ed2-a8d8-1b0146746e07","timestamp":"2026-09-28T20:25:13.447Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"e054b45d-33cd-4562-af51-7c3370696c58","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\Flint\\.claude\\worktrees\\step1-triage","sessionId":"e054b45d-33cd-4562-af51-7c3370696c58","version":"2.1.283","gitBranch":"step1-triage"}
