er only, full profile? →`MatchupAnalysis_FB2026/docs/`\n- **PP Recruiting (9/26)**: 013 built; size Q + 011 await Mauro (asst GM). →`PP_Recruiting/docs/`\n- **Sleep sched (9/16)**: R1 merged; NEXT night/early-kickoff. →`sleep-scheduler/`\n- **TypeSafe (9/26)**: gate log-only, review ~10/6; Drive-triage prereg #30. NEXT: Y/Ns 22 surgeries. →`TypeSafe_Sandbox/docs/`\n- **Flint (9/26)**: sport-sci KB, side lane. Harries in vault; 7 staged, fixes pending. →`Flint/docs/STATUS.md`\n- **PFF DB (9/22)**: swap Parquet on Drive, never the DB. Both: 2026 thru wk3 + video. →`PFF_Data_Project/docs/`\n\n## Environment Notes\n- Hooks: patch both copies only for shared events; Codex has no prompt-submit event. →Tier A hook-two-copies-trap.\n- daily-backup: manifest entries alone copy nothing; sweep nested ~/.claude repos →handoff 09-19.\n- `DEV/Linda Projects` = private I-983 repo; folder has a space, repo an underscore.\n- `~/DEV` = THIN repo; `.gitignore` starts `/*` — never remove. →Tier A github-consolidation.\n- Win: `Desktop\\DEV` syncs via Drive (robocopy retired 9/22). No large DBs/junctions: renv via `RENV_PATHS_LIBRARY_ROOT`, PFF via `PFF_DB`.\n- Schedules →automation-cadence. CFB capture Mac only. Dashboard →command-centre.\n- Post-merge: delete merged branches/worktrees unasked (verify first) →Tier A post-merge-cleanup.\n\n## Pending Decisions\n- **OKR gate (9/14)**: AI buy-in + data governance (Anthony = outside-firm adviser, NOT Mauro). NCAA charter or park?\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":12,"oldLines":8,"newStart":12,"newLines":8,"lines":[" - **FB matchups (9/23)**: EPA = PFF via `scripts/pff_epa_profile.py`. Wk4 COLO: EPA layer only, full profile? →`MatchupAnalysis_FB2026/docs/`"," - **PP Recruiting (9/26)**: 013 built; size Q + 011 await Mauro (asst GM). →`PP_Recruiting/docs/`"," - **Sleep sched (9/16)**: R1 merged; NEXT night/early-kickoff. →`sleep-scheduler/`","-- **TypeSafe (9/26)**: gate log-only, review ~10/6; Drive-triage prereg #30. NEXT: Y/Ns 22 surgeries. →`TypeSafe_Sandbox/docs/`","-- **Flint (9/26)**: sport-sci KB, side lane. Harries in vault; 7 staged, fixes pending. →`Flint/docs/STATUS.md`","+- **TypeSafe (9/28)**: Drive triage FAIL 76.5%; Jev>Haiku, used for Flint. PR #31 draft; Eric audit. →`TypeSafe_Sandbox/docs/`","+- **Flint (9/28)**: interview done+applied. NEXT Eric: shortlists, primer, CVASPS. →`Flint/docs/STATUS.md`"," - **PFF DB (9/22)**: swap Parquet on Drive, never the DB. Both: 2026 thru wk3 + video. →`PFF_Data_Project/docs/`"," "," ## Environment Notes"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false,"contentNotInModelContext":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0dac66c2-5285-4fb7-9524-a5e6dc87667b","session_id":"e054b45d-33cd-4562-af51-7c3370696c58","sessionKind":"bg","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV","sessionId":"e054b45d-33cd-4562-af51-7c3370696c58","version":"2.1.283","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"26d28d08-c462-47e0-acab-72b139e855a0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfWUctD6nR3e3dysYacDR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WtfM646Rtvx7VcNWZ3kYHS","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\Flint\\.claude\\worktrees\\step1-triage\\docs\\handoffs\\2026-09-28-flint-day3-evening.md","content":"# Handoff: 2026-09-28 evening (Flint interview + Jev pilot scored)\n\nResume here on 2026-09-29. Two repos were touched: Flint (`step1-triage`) and\nTypeSafe_Sandbox (`worktree-drive-triage-run`, draft PR #31). Both are pushed.\n\n## What happened today\n\n1. **Jev Drive-triage pilot scored** (TypeSafe, tenth measurement). FAIL on the 90% domain\n   accuracy bar (127/166, 76.5%). Jev beat Haiku (127 vs 108 on its confident subset) and,\n   on the unclassified half that Flint needs, beat Codex (81 vs 75 of 100). **Eric's decision:\n   Jev does Flint's pass, with his shortlist approval kept as the check.** Write-up:\n   `TypeSafe_Sandbox/docs/STATUS.md`, `docs/JEV_CAPABILITY_MAP.md` (new prereg rule: state what\n   happens when the model fails its bar but beats every comparator), `drive_triage/results.md`.\n2. **Method interview done** (30 questions: the 27 in `docs/interview-prep.md` plus the 6\n   peaking questions, overlaps merged). Answers in Eric's words:\n   `docs/interview/2026-09-28-method-interview.md`. Applied to `docs/method-baseline.md` and\n   the peaking synthesis, now rev 3 (`docs/synthesis/peaking-and-taper-in-season-football.md`).\n3. **RTP templates staged**: `staging/rtp/Baylor {UE,LE} Rehab Program Template.{docx,md}`\n   (gitignored). Originals moved to Drive\n   `01_PROJECTS/_ACTIVE/HighPerformanceInitative_RTP/Docs/` (April copies kept with a\n   `_2026-04-15` suffix).\n4. **Constraints-led approach primer** for Eric (interview Q25):\n   `docs/primers/constraints-led-approach.md`.\n5. The Sep 26 session's stopped jobs were checked: the OCR (Francis, CFTS, Zatsiorsky 2e) and\n   the CVASPS transcription had already finished on 9/27. Only the whole-Drive catalog is\n   outstanding, and it is **held until Eric approves the shortlists** (Eric's call, option a),\n   because a re-run overwrites `data/manifest.csv` and the triage behind the shortlists.\n\n## Waiting on Eric (tomorrow morning)\n\n1. **Approve the shortlists**: `docs/shortlists/README.md` (8 decisions) plus the 14 discipline\n   files. Then move approved sources into `docs/QUEUE.md` and re-run the catalog\n   (`pwsh -NoProfile -File scripts/build_manifest.ps1 *> data/run_wide.log`, then\n   `uv run scripts/triage_rules.py`; it starts over and takes hours; do not use `-Only`).\n2. **Jev blind audit**: `TypeSafe_Sandbox/.claude/worktrees/drive-triage-run/drive_triage/private/audit_sheet.md`,\n   A/B/N on each of 20 Verdict lines. Then score it next to the original (never changes the\n   verdict) and update PR #31. The unblinding map is `private/audit_key.json`; never show it first.\n3. **Read the primer** and answer its three questions.\n4. **CVASPS listening**: section 2 of `docs/cvasps-corroboration-proposals.md` (47 rows with\n   timestamps), low-confidence rows first. Audio: `staging/audio/landonevans...wav`.\n\n## Next for a session (no Eric input needed)\n\n- DSI (CMJ vs IMTP) evidence check before any synthesis cites it (Eric uses DSI, not SJ-CMJ).\n- Open tensions from the interview are in the baseline's tensions section: Wednesday vs daily\n  mRSI; COD and FMS gates in the RTP templates vs \"we don't test COD\" / \"screens change\n  nothing\"; %1RM charts with no 1RM testing; Q22 \"we don't assess readiness\".\n- `_work/review_peaking_synthesis_opus.md` revision log still stops at rev 2.\n- Codex rescue note: the RTP CLA course is missing two sources (Myszka PDF not in `sources/`,\n  Bobrownicki not in Zotero); Joe has not done lesson 0001's field task.\n\n## Machine and memory\n\n- **memsearch drain scheduled 2026-09-28 17:30** (`\\Eric\\memsearch-drain-once`, WakeToRun,\n  20 h limit). The 12:01 run died within a minute (0xC000013A) and indexed nothing. Check\n  tomorrow: `~/.claude/scripts/logs/memsearch-drain.log` should end with an `exit=0` line; the\n  backlog was about 10,100 chunks at about 5 s each (about 14 h).\n- Background jobs on this laptop get killed by Claude Code's low-memory reaper when the\n  session is idle. Long comparator runs finished reliably as foreground chunks (7 files of\n  about 70 s each per call, under the 10-minute tool limit).\n- Headless `claude -p` runs (the Haiku comparator) each fired the memsearch SessionEnd hook;\n  the hook now skips SDK sessions, but prefer `codex exec` or an API key for bulk runs.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1856,"cache_read_input_tokens":270557,"output_tokens":2413,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":32},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1856,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2413,"cache_read_input_tokens":270557,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1856,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1856},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01WtfM646Rtvx7VcNWZ3kYHS":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\eric_rash\\Desktop\\DEV\\Flint\\.claude\\worktrees\\step1-triage\\docs\\handoffs\\2026-09-28-flint-day3-evening.md","content":"# Handoff: 2026-09-28 evening (Flint interview + Jev pilot scored)\n\nResume here on 2026-09-29. Two repos were touched: Flint (`step1-triage`) and\nTypeSafe_Sandbox (`worktree-drive-triage-run`, draft PR #31). Both are pushed.\n\n## What happened today\n\n1. **Jev Dr